{"type":"thinking","text":"Let me start by understanding the task. I'm dispatched as a deep-review agent to run a detached fan-out lineage for a deep-review workflow on a spec folder. I need to:\n\n1. Read the workflow YAML and SKILL.md\n2. Bind artifact_dir to the lineage directory\n3. Run phase_init, phase_main_loop (up to 5 iterations, convergence 0.1), phase_synthesis\n4. Write all files only in specs/system-speckit/spec-folder-tooling/005-subtrack-proposal-and-archive-reach/review/lineages/dsh-2\n5. Output FANOUT_LINEAGE_COMPLETE:dsh-2\n\nLet me first explore the repository structure and read the required files.\n\nWait — the working directory is already the lineage directory. Interesting. Let me check what's there.\n\nLet me read the key files:\n- .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/SKILL.md\n- .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl\n- The workflow YAML (maybe .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml or a fanout workflow)\n- The steer.md if exists\n- Existing state files in the lineage directory\n\nLet me start."}
