{"type":"tool_result","callId":"call_1664d14da6c4409992d1ffca","status":"completed","result":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n2060:               GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n2061:               [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n2062:               EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-iteration-error.XXXXXX\")\"\n2063:               cat <<'DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD' > \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n2064:               {\"stem\":\"deep_review.iteration_error\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\"},\"data\":{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":{current_iteration},\"run\":{current_iteration},\"mode\":\"review\",\"status\":\"error\",\"focus\":\"{next_dimension}\",\"dimensions\":[\"{next_dimension}\"],\"filesReviewed\":[],\"findingsCount\":0,\"findingsSummary\":{\"P0\":0,\"P1\":0,\"P2\":0},\"findingsNew\":{\"P0\":0,\"P1\":0,\"P2\":0},\"findingDetails\":[],\"traceabilityChecks\":{\"summary\":{\"required\":0,\"executed\":0,\"pass\":0,\"partial\":0,\"fail\":0,\"blocked\":0,\"notApplicable\":0,\"gatingFailures\":0},\"results\":[]},\"newFindingsRatio\":0.0,\"durationMs\":0,\"sessionId\":\"{config.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.generation},\"lineageMode\":\"{config.lineageMode}\"}}\n2065:               DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD\n2066:               node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n2067:               RECORD_STATUS=$?\n2068:               rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n2069:               exit \"$RECORD_STATUS\"\n2070: \n2071:       step_post_iteration_claim_adjudication:\n2072:         action: \"Validate typed claim-adjudication packets for any new P0/P1 findings and persist the result to state.jsonl so the next iteration's claimAdjudicationGate can read it\"\n2073:         verify:\n2074:           - typed_packets_present: \"Every new P0/P1 finding in review/iterations/iteration-{NNN}.md contains a claim-adjudication JSON block\"\n2075:           - packet_fields: \"Each packet includes claim, evidenceRefs, counterevidenceSought, alternativeExplanation, finalSeverity, confidence, downgradeTrigger\"\n2076:           - missing_packet_ids: \"List of new P0/P1 finding IDs that are missing a typed packet or field; empty array when all packets validate\"\n2077:         on_pass:\n2078:           set:\n2079:             claim_adjudication_passed: true\n2080:           # The row is staged as a canonical ledger event and appended by the gateway:\n2081:           # the state log is a projection of the ledger, so a write beside it is dropped\n2082:           # by the next refresh.\n2083:           command: |\n2084:             GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n2085:             [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n2086:             EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-claim-adjudication.XXXXXX\")\"\n2087:             cat <<'DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD' > \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n2088:             {\"stem\":\"deep_review.claim_adjudication\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\"},\"data\":{\"mode\":\"review\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"passed\":true,\"activeP0P1\":{active_p0_p1_count},\"missingPackets\":[],\"reason\":null,\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}}}\n2089:             DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD\n2090:             node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n2091:             RECORD_STATUS=$?\n2092:             rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n2093:             exit \"$RECORD_STATUS\"\n2094:           log: \"Claim adjudication passed for iteration {current_iteration}. All new P0/P1 findings have typed packets.\"\n2095:         on_fail:\n2096:           action: \"Mark the iteration as invalid for convergence. The next iteration's claimAdjudicationGate (step_check_convergence step 0) reads the persisted `passed: false` event and vetoes STOP until a follow-up iteration rewrites the packets.\"\n2097:           set:\n2098:             claim_adjudication_passed: false\n2099:           command: |\n2100:             GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n2101:             [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n2102:             EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-claim-adjudication.XXXXXX\")\"\n2103:             cat <<'DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD' > \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n2104:             {\"stem\":\"deep_review.claim_adjudication\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\"},\"data\":{\"mode\":\"review\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"passed\":false,\"activeP0P1\":{active_p0_p1_count},\"missingPackets\":{missing_packet_ids},\"reason\":\"Missing typed packet fields for new P0/P1 findings\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}}}\n2105:             DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD\n2106:             node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n2107:             RECORD_STATUS=$?\n2108:             rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n2109:             exit \"$RECORD_STATUS\"\n2110:           log: \"Claim adjudication incomplete for new P0/P1 findings. Event persisted. The next iteration's step_check_convergence claim-adjudication pre-check will veto STOP while `passed: false` remains the latest event and active P0/P1 > 0.\"\n2111: \n2112:       step_reduce_review_state:\n2113:         action: \"Run reducer to refresh the canonical findings registry before dashboard generation\"\n2114:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors\"\n2115:         read:\n2116:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n2117:           - \"{state_paths.iteration_pattern}\"\n2118:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n2119:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n2120:         write:\n2121:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n2122:           - \"{state_paths.dashboard}\"\n2123:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n2124:         failure_modes:\n2125:           malformed_delta: \"skip + warn\"\n2126:           missing_iteration_file: \"no-op + error\"\n2127:           schema_mismatch: \"reject + conflict event\"\n2128:         guarantee: \"Idempotent for identical inputs\"\n2129:         note: \"Reducer outputs findingsRegistry, dashboardMetrics, and strategyUpdates. Re-running the same inputs must be idempotent.\"\n2130: \n2131:       step_graph_upsert:\n2132:         action: \"Project canonical review coverage plus optional graphEvents into graph nodes and edges, then upsert it\"\n2133:         read:\n2134:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2135:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n2136:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n2137:         transform: |\n2138:           1. Read the latest iteration JSONL record after reducer completion.\n2139:           2. Seed one stable DIMENSION node for every configured review dimension, falling back to correctness, security, traceability, and maintainability.\n2140:           3. Seed one stable FILE node for every latest-record filesReviewed entry and emit a COVERS edge from each latest-record dimension to each reviewed file.\n2141:           4. Merge optional graphEvents nodes after normalizing type = uppercase(event.kind || event.nodeKind || event.type); keep only DIMENSION, FILE, FINDING, EVIDENCE, REMEDIATION, BUG_CLASS, INVARIANT, PRODUCER, CONSUMER, TEST.\n2142:           5. Merge optional graphEvents edges after normalizing relation = uppercase(event.relation); keep only COVERS, EVIDENCE_FOR, CONTRADICTS, RESOLVES, CONFIRMS, ESCALATES, IN_DIMENSION, IN_FILE.\n2143:           6. Emit nodes as { id, type, name, iteration, metadata } and edges as { id, relation, sourceId, targetId, metadata }, deduplicated by id.\n2144:           7. Discard malformed or unknown optional events without discarding canonical dimension and file coverage.\n2145:         bash: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs --spec-folder \\\"{spec_folder}\\\" --loop-type \\\"review\\\" --session-id \\\"{session_id}\\\" --nodes '{graph_nodes_json}' --edges '{graph_edges_json}'\"\n2146:         note: \"Invoke the runtime script directly. Canonical iteration fields provide baseline coverage; graphEvents ad","truncated":true}
