{"type":"thinking","text":"Now I understand the workflow. I'm executing the fan-out lineage: I should run phase_init, phase_main_loop (up to 5 iterations or convergence), and phase_synthesis. Since I'm a fan-out lineage, step_fanout_spawn is skipped (already satisfied), step_fanout_merge is skipped when config.fanout absent in lineage config (the lineage's own config likely won't have fanout), step_emit_resource_map skip_when fanout is present (lineage config may have fanout? need to check the lineage's config).\n\nWait — the lineage directory currently only has invocation-metadata.json, audit/effect ledgers, containment, locks, .executor-state. No config yet. So I need to run init.\n\nLet me check the steer.md — the prompt says to read it when it exists. It's not there yet. I'll check again before each iteration.\n\nLet me also read the state-format reference and review-core doctrine, and the deep-review-strategy template, config template, findings registry format, and the reducer usage. Also check the fanout-run.cjs to see how lineage config is generated (to know what fields exist, e.g., fanout flag). Let me grep fanout-run.cjs for lineage config creation.\n\nAlso, importantly: my write surface is ONLY the lineage directory. The workflow steps that write outside it (e.g., step_apply_lifecycle_request, step_migrate_legacy_review_state, step_generate_context, step_stage_artifact_dir) must be skipped or adapted. My review target is the spec folder, read-only. I must not run validate.sh or generate-context.js.\n\nI need to figure out:\n1. Init: create config in lineage dir, state log via gateway, findings registry, strategy, directories, maybe resource-map detection.\n2. Loop: 5 iterations max. Dimensions: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability. Plus the operator review focus (documentation alignment). Since only 5 iterations and 4 dimensions, I can combine: Iteration 1 correctness (perhaps with docs), 2 security, 3 traceability (docs alignment focused), 4 maintainability (docs alignment), 5 cross-reference / docs alignment. The review_focus is docs alignment against skills. The most valuable finding: docs stale against phases 006-010 behavior.\n\n3. Each iteration: write iteration-NNN.md, delta, strategy update, gateway append, reducer.\n4. Synthesis: derive verdict, resource map (emit skip? the lineage config likely not fanout, hmm; step_emit_resource_map skip_when config.fanout is present — lineage config might include fanout to make merge work; let me check fanout-run.cjs), compile review-report.md in lineage, convergence report via synthesis-closeout.cjs, update config status complete. The synthesis closeout writes to state log through gateway; it may write dashboard etc. It takes artifact dir. It might write review-report? It takes --output (review_output) and --dashboard. That's fine, inside lineage.\n\nLet me inspect fanout-run.cjs and the state-format/reducer to understand expected artifacts. Let me also check if there's a previous lineage run (dsh-1) in progress that I can look at as an example — reading is allowed. dsh-1 currently has the same dirs. Maybe both started at the same time; dsh-1 may not have files yet. Let me check.\n\nAlso, I need to find out what the review target files are. The goal-file-manifest.txt contains the scope. Let me read it. And read the spec folder's spec.md, goal.md. The review focus says scope is exactly goal-file-manifest.txt.\n\nLet me start with init. But first read state-format.md and the strategy template, and the config template. Also the reducer's expectations (delta schema). Let me read those."}
