{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-a6f154b5b75fc0fc","status":"completed","result":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-format.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Review State Format\n3: description: State file schemas for the autonomous deep review loop, config, JSONL log, strategy, iteration files, and review report.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"deep review state format\"\n6:   - \"deep review config schema\"\n7:   - \"review severity weights\"\n8:   - \"file protection levels\"\n9:   - \"review iteration file structure\"\n10: importance_tier: important\n11: contextType: implementation\n12: version: 1.11.1.0\n13: ---\n14: \n15: # Deep Review State Format\n16: \n17: State file schemas for the autonomous deep review loop.\n18: \n19: ---\n20: \n21: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n22: \n23: ### Purpose\n24: \n25: The review packet is reproduced from disk on every resume, so each file's format, mutability, and fields are pinned here for the reducer, the dashboard, the validator, and the resume path.\n26: \n27: ### When to Use\n28: \n29: - Validating deep-review state files emitted by an iteration or by the reducer.\n30: - Implementing a state consumer (e.g. dashboard, advisor probe, downstream packet).\n31: - Debugging JSONL reducer output or auditing schema-version transitions.\n32: - Authoring fixtures that need to round-trip through the reducer.\n33: \n34: The deep review loop uses 9 state files under the resolved `{artifact_dir}/` owned by the target spec:\n35: \n36: | File | Format | Mutability |\n37: |------|--------|------------|\n38: | `deep-review-config.json` | JSON | Immutable after init, except the terminal `status: complete` flip |\n39: | `deep-review-state.jsonl` | JSON Lines | Append-only |\n40: | `deep-review-findings-registry.json` | JSON | Auto-generated reducer state |\n41: | `deep-review-strategy.md` | Markdown | Updated each iteration |\n42: | `deep-review-dashboard.md` | Markdown | Auto-generated (read-only) |\n43: | `.deep-review-pause` | Sentinel | Created/deleted by user |\n44: | `resource-map.md` | Markdown | Emitted once at synthesis unless `resource_map.emit` is false |\n45: | `review-report.md` | Markdown | Updated at synthesis |\n46: | `iterations/iteration-NNN.md` | Markdown | Write-once |\n47: \n48: ```text\n49: {artifact_dir}/\n50:   deep-review-config.json\n51:   deep-review-state.jsonl\n52:   deep-review-findings-registry.json\n53:   deep-review-strategy.md\n54:   deep-review-dashboard.md\n55:   .deep-review-pause\n56:   review-report.md\n57:   iterations/\n58:     iteration-001.md\n59:     iteration-002.md\n60:     ...\n61: ```\n62: \n63: `{artifact_dir}` comes from `resolveArtifactRoot(specFolder, 'review')`. Root-spec runs resolve directly to `{spec_folder}/review/`. Child-phase and sub-phase runs use **flat-first**: a first run with an empty `review/` resolves directly to `{spec_folder}/review/` (no `pt-NN` wrapper). A `pt-NN` packet is allocated only when prior content for a non-matching target already exists. Continuation runs reuse the existing flat artifact (or matching `pt-NN` packet). This avoids the unnecessary `pt-01` wrapper on first runs.\n64: \n65: Example (first run on a child phase): `.../026-graph.../006-continuity-refactor-gates/003-gate-c-writer-ready/` → `003-gate-c-writer-ready/review/` (flat, no subfolder).\n66: \n67: Example (subsequent run with prior content for a different target): `003-gate-c-writer-ready/review/003-gate-c-writer-ready-pt-02/` (`pt-NN` allocated as a sibling to the prior content; subfolder name is `{basename(spec_folder)}-pt-{NN}`).\n68: \n69: ---\n70: \n71: ## 2. CONFIG FILE (deep-review-config.json)\n72: \n73: Created during initialization. Not modified after creation.\n74: \n75: ```json\n76: {\n77:   \"topic\": \"Review of deep-review skill package\",\n78:   \"mode\": \"review\",\n79:   \"reviewTarget\": \"specs/030-deep-review-review-mode\",\n80:   \"reviewTargetType\": \"spec-folder\",\n81:   \"reviewDimensions\": [\"correctness\", \"security\", \"traceability\", \"maintainability\"],\n82:   \"resource_map_present\": false,\n83:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-04-03T12-00-00Z\",\n84:   \"parentSessionId\": null,\n85:   \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n86:   \"generation\": 1,\n87:   \"continuedFromRun\": null,\n88:   \"maxIterations\": 7,\n89:   \"convergenceThreshold\": 0.10,\n90:   \"stuckThreshold\": 2,\n91:   \"severityThreshold\": \"P2\",\n92:   \"crossReference\": {\n93:     \"core\": [\"spec_code\", \"checklist_evidence\"],\n94:     \"overlay\": [\"feature_catalog_code\", \"playbook_capability\"]\n95:   },\n96:   \"qualityGateThreshold\": true,\n97:   \"releaseReadinessState\": \"in-progress\",\n98:   \"specFolder\": \"030-deep-review-review-mode\",\n99:   \"createdAt\": \"2026-03-24T14:00:00Z\",\n100:   \"status\": \"initialized\",\n101:   \"executionMode\": \"auto\",\n102:   \"fileProtection\": {\n103:     \"deep-review-config.json\": \"immutable\",\n104:     \"deep-review-state.jsonl\": \"append-only\",\n105:     \"deep-review-findings-registry.json\": \"auto-generated\",\n106:     \"deep-review-strategy.md\": \"mutable\",\n107:     \"deep-review-dashboard.md\": \"auto-generated\",\n108:     \".deep-review-pause\": \"operator-controlled\",\n109:     \"review-report.md\": \"mutable\",\n110:     \"review-report-v*.md\": \"write-once\",\n111:     \"iteration-*.md\": \"write-once\"\n112:   },\n113:   \"reducer\": {\n114:     \"enabled\": true,\n115:     \"inputs\": [\"latestJSONLDelta\", \"newIterationFile\", \"priorReducedState\"],\n116:     \"outputs\": [\"findingsRegistry\", \"dashboardMetrics\", \"strategyUpdates\"],\n117:     \"metrics\": [\n118:       \"dimensionsCovered\",\n119:       \"findingsBySeverity\",\n120:       \"openFindings\",\n121:       \"resolvedFindings\",\n122:       \"convergenceScore\"\n123:     ]\n124:   }\n125: }\n126: ```\n127: \n128: ### Field Reference\n129: \n130: | Field | Type | Default | Description |\n131: |-------|------|---------|-------------|\n132: | mode | `\"review\"` | -- | Session mode discriminator (required) |\n133: | reviewTarget | string | -- | Path or identifier of the review target |\n134: | reviewTargetType | string | `\"spec-folder\"` | `spec-folder`, `skill`, `agent`, `track`, `files` |\n135: | reviewDimensions | string[] | all 4 | Dimensions to evaluate |\n136: | resource_map_present | boolean | false | True only when `{specFolder}/resource-map.md` existed during init, enables the Resource Map Coverage audit pass and conditional report section |\n137: | sessionId | string | -- | Stable identifier for the current review lineage |\n138: | parentSessionId | string \\| null | `null` | Parent lineage reference for restart flows |\n139: | lineageMode | string | `\"new\"` | `new`, `resume`, `restart`. `fork` and `completed-continue` are deferred and not emitted by the current runtime |\n140: | generation | number | 1 | Lineage generation number, incremented on `restart`, unchanged on `resume` |\n141: | continuedFromRun | number \\| null | `null` | Count of completed iteration records at the lifecycle boundary (set on `resume` and `restart`) |\n142: | maxIterations | number | 7 | Hard cap on loop iterations |\n143: | convergenceThreshold | number | 0.10 | Stop when severity-weighted new findings ratio below this |\n144: | stuckThreshold | number | 2 | Consecutive no-progress iterations before recovery |\n145: | severityThreshold | string | `\"P2\"` | Minimum severity to report: `P0`, `P1`, `P2` |\n146: | crossReference | object | -- | Core (hard-gated) and overlay (advisory) protocol sets |\n147: | qualityGateThreshold | boolean | true | Whether binary quality gates are enforced |\n148: | specFolder | string | -- | Spec folder path (relative to specs/) |\n149: | status | string | `\"initialized\"` | `initialized`, `running`, `converged`, `stuck`, `complete`, `error` |\n150: | releaseReadinessState | string | `\"in-progress\"` | `in-progress`, `converged`, `release-blocking` |\n151: | fileProtection | object | -- | Mutability declarations (see protection levels below) |\n152: | reducer | object | -- | Canonical reducer inputs, outputs, and metrics names |\n153: \n154: ### File Protection Levels\n155: \n156: | Level | Meaning |\n157: |-------|---------|\n158: | immutable | Cannot be modified after creation (config: the terminal `status: complete` flip is the one permitted write) |\n159: | append-only | New content added at end only |\n160: | mutable | Can be read, edited, overwritten |\n161: | write-once | Created once, never modified |\n","truncated":true}
