{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-8de47f0bfa1f28aa","status":"completed","result":"=== 006-relocate-resume-and-preflight/spec.md\n---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Phase 6: relocate-resume-and-preflight\"\ndescription: \"A relocate.mjs run that stops partway cannot always be finished by rerunning the same map, and its preflight accepts a source that never existed and two spellings of one folder. This phase makes the rerun finish every step and makes the preflight refuse both inputs.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"relocate resume and preflight\"\n  - \"phase 6 relocate resume and preflight\"\n  - \"relocate rerun finishes late steps\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core | v2.4 -->\n# Feature Specification: Phase 6: relocate-resume-and-preflight\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n---\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 1 |\n| **Priority** | P1 |\n| **Status** | Complete |\n| **Created** | 2026-11-14 |\n| **Branch** | `worktrees/375-subtrack-review-remediation` |\n| **Parent Spec** | ../spec.md |\n| **Phase** | 6 of 10 |\n| **Predecessor** | 005-tests-and-closeout |\n| **Successor** | 007-phase-map-and-prearchive-rewrites |\n| **Handoff Criteria** | After a late step fails once, a second `relocate.mjs --apply` of the same map prints that step as `ok` and exits 0, and a third run prints `relocate: nothing to do` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n---\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-context -->\n## Phase Context\nThis is **Phase 6** of the Subtrack proposal, deterministic packet relocation, z_archive on every subtrack and opt-in archive search specification.\n**Scope Boundary**: Resume and preflight state inside `relocate.mjs` and its suite. No reference rewrite rule, no `archive.sh` change and no `create.sh` change.\n**Dependencies**:\n- The two code reviews of 2026-11-14 in `../scratch/`, which name the findings this phase closes\n- The stubbed harness in `runtime/cli/tests/relocate.vitest.ts`, which this phase extends with stubs that fail once\n**Deliverables**:\n- A rerun that finishes the redirect table, the trigger index and the sweep of the close after any of them failed\n- A rerun that completes a half-finished move step and a failed identity step\n- A preflight that refuses a source that never existed and two spellings of one folder\n- Suite cases for each of the above\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-context -->\n---\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n### Problem Statement\n`relocate.mjs` tells the operator to rerun the same map after a failed step, but the rerun cannot always finish the work. The work check below has no term for the redirect table, the trigger index or the close, so a rerun after one of them failed prints `nothing to do` and exits 0. A half-finished move step is refused by the tool's own dirty-tree check, a failed identity step is skipped when the folder kept its name, and the preflight reads a mistyped source as a finished move and two case spellings of one folder as two folders.\n### Purpose\nRerunning the same map after any failed step finishes that step, and the preflight refuses a map that names a source that never existed or names one folder twice.\n=== 007-phase-map-and-prearchive-rewrites/spec.md\n---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Phase 7: phase-map-and-prearchive-rewrites\"\ndescription: \"relocate.mjs rewrites a packet id only where it is written in full, so a renumbered phase leaves its parent's phase map naming a folder that is gone, and a restore onto a new number leaves references to the id the packet had before it was archived. This phase adds both rewrites.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"phase map and prearchive rewrites\"\n  - \"phase 7 phase map and prearchive rewrites\"\n  - \"bare sibling folder name in a phase map\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core | v2.4 -->\n# Feature Specification: Phase 7: phase-map-and-prearchive-rewrites\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n---\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 1 |\n| **Priority** | P1 |\n| **Status** | Complete |\n| **Created** | 2026-11-14 |\n| **Branch** | `worktrees/375-subtrack-review-remediation` |\n| **Parent Spec** | ../spec.md |\n| **Phase** | 7 of 10 |\n| **Predecessor** | 006-relocate-resume-and-preflight |\n| **Successor** | 008-restore-and-phase-numbering |\n| **Handoff Criteria** | After `relocate.mjs --renumber <phase parent> --apply`, `rg` for the old folder name in the parent's `spec.md` prints nothing |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n---\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-context -->\n## Phase Context\nThis is **Phase 7** of the Subtrack proposal, deterministic packet relocation, z_archive on every subtrack and opt-in archive search specification.\n**Scope Boundary**: The reference rewrites of `relocate.mjs`, section 6 of the script. No resume logic, no `archive.sh` exit handling and no `create.sh` change.\n**Dependencies**:\n- Phase 006, committed, because it edits the same script\n- Decision D3 of the parent goal: moving or renumbering a packet needs no hand edits\n**Deliverables**:\n- A rewrite of bare sibling folder names inside a phase parent's own documents\n- A rewrite of the id a packet had before it was archived, when it leaves `z_archive/` under a new number\n- Suite cases for both\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-context -->\n---\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n### Problem Statement\n`relocate.mjs` finds an old id with the pattern below, which matches a multi-segment id or a root packet after `specs/`. A phase parent names its children by bare folder name, in the Phase Documentation Map, the handoff table and each child's Predecessor and Successor rows, so a renumbered phase leaves those rows naming a folder that is gone while the run exits 0 and strict validation passes. A packet restored from `z_archive/` onto a new number has the same gap: only the `z_archive` spelling of its id is rewritten, and references written before it was archived still name the old id.\n### Purpose\nAfter a renumber, a re-parent or a renumbering restore, no document names the moved folder by a name it no longer has, with no hand edit.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n=== 008-restore-and-phase-numbering/spec.md\n---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Phase 8: restore-and-phase-numbering\"\ndescription: \"archive.sh reports a failed restore after every step landed, restores a track-level packet into a track that holds sub-tracks, and create.sh reuses the number of an archived phase. This phase fixes the restore verdict, refuses the mixed track and counts archived phases.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"restore and phase numbering\"\n  - \"phase 8 restore and phase numbering\"\n  - \"phase numbering counts archived phases\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core | v2.4 -->\n# Feature Specification: Phase 8: restore-and-phase-numbering\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n---\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 1 |\n| **Priority** | P1 |\n| **Status** | Complete |\n| **Created** | 2026-11-14 |\n| **Branch** | `worktrees/375-subtrack-review-remediation` |\n| **Parent Spec** | ../spec.md |\n| **Phase** | 8 of 10 |\n| **Predecessor** | 007-phase-map-and-prearchive-rewrites |\n| **Successor** | 009-proposal-search-and-routing |\n| **Handoff Criteria** | With `001-alpha` live and `z_archive/002-gamma` archived in a phase parent, `create.sh --phase --parent` creates `003-*` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n---\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-context -->\n## Phase Context\nThis is **Phase 8** of the Subtrack proposal, deterministic packet relocation, z_archive on every subtrack and opt-in archive search specification.\n**Scope Boundary**: The restore path of `archive.sh`, the one exit status of `relocate.mjs` that the restore reads with the README row that states it, and the phase numbering loop of `create.sh`. No rewrite rule and no search change.\n**Dependencies**:\n- Phase 006, which decides when a rerun runs the close again: only until the sweep has passed once. A run that ends on the status this phase adds has landed in that sense\n- Phase 007, committed, because it changes `relocate.mjs` and the shared `archive-track.vitest.ts`, which this phase also edits\n- Decisions D2 and D4 of the parent goal: mixed tracks stay forbidden, a","truncated":true}
