{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-aa055adc1fe96bdb","status":"completed","result":"4:allowed-tools: [Bash, Edit, Glob, Grep, Read, Task, Write]\n24:- **Contents**: Markdown files (spec.md, plan.md, tasks.md, and implementation-summary.md when work is complete) plus optional support folders such as `scratch/`, `research/`, or `review/`\n34:- Templates, knowledge base, build/tooling files\n61:Any agent writing authored spec folder docs MUST use contract-backed templates through `create.sh` or the inline renderer.\n66:Run `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <spec-folder> --strict --quiet` once after the last authored spec-doc write and before completion claims.\n70:The template rule exempts workflow-owned deep-research packet markdown: `research/iterations/*.md`, `research/deep-research-*.md` and progressive `research/research.md` loop updates.\n71:`/deep:research` must run targeted strict validation after every `spec.md` mutation it performs.\n72:@deep-research exclusively writes `research/research.md`. @debug exclusively writes `debug-delegation.md`.\n83:| `debug-delegation.md` | \"stuck\", \"can't fix\", \"tried everything\", \"same error\", \"fresh eyes\", \"hours on this\", \"still failing\", \"need help debugging\" | Suggest Task-tool debug delegation |\n119:| Enforced by | `check-completion.sh` | `AC_CLOSURE` and `AC_COVERAGE` in `validate.sh` |\n124:`acceptance-criteria.md` is an optional add-on: `validate.sh` warns when a Level 2+ packet has none. Once the file exists, `AC_CLOSURE` is an error-severity gate on that packet.\n129:Gate 1 resolves a prompt against the committed trigger index with `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/lookup-trigger-index.mjs --json -- \"<prompt>\"`.\n134:[`references/structure/grep-convention.md`](references/structure/grep-convention.md) holds the frontmatter, anchor, naming and body-preservation rules. `validate.sh` enforces them on every spec document.\n144:Saves go through `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js`, invoked by `/speckit:save`.\n150:Regenerate the index with `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/generate-trigger-index.mjs` after spec-doc frontmatter changes. The artifact at `runtime/data/trigger-index.json` is committed, so a fresh clone answers Gate 1 before anything is built.\n173:Run `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <spec-folder> --strict` before completion claims.\n179:- **Repair and revalidation:** `validate.sh` then applies the repair once, prints each rewritten file and validates again.\n181:- **Child validator behavior:** Child validator runs inside read-only tools set it to `0`.\n189:- **OpenCode plugin contract:** The OpenCode surface is `.opencode/plugins/opencode-goal.js` and `.opencode/commands/goal-opencode.md`. It injects with `experimental.chat.system.transform` and observes lifecycle events through the plugin `event` hook. It exposes `opencode_goal` / `opencode_goal_status` plugin tools. Use [`.skilled/hooks/goal/goal-plugin.md`](../../hooks/goal/goal-plugin.md) for the operator contract, restart requirement, environment variables, validation commands and boundary between raw `objective` and generated `goalPrompt`.\n201:2. **Scaffold from contract-backed templates** - Use `create.sh` or `inline-gate-renderer`, NEVER create from scratch\n211:12. **Run validate.sh before completion** - Completion Verification requirement\n213:14. **Suggest /speckit:save when session-end keywords detected OR after extended work (15+ tool calls)** - Proactive context preservation\n214:15. **Suggest Task-tool debug delegation after 3+ failed fix attempts on same error** - Do not continue without offering a fresh debugging pass\n228:19. **Enforce ToC policy from validation rules** - Only `research/research.md` may include a Table of Contents section; remove ToC headings from standard spec artifacts\n241:    - Documentation-layer guidance: `validate.sh` does not lint slugs today (operator decision; may be lifted in a follow-on packet).\n272:Success means the selected spec folder uses the right template set, placeholders and sample content are removed, links between packet docs work, continuity is saved or updated, Level 2+ `tasks.md` P0/P1 checklist items are verified with evidence, every `acceptance-criteria.md` criterion is `Met`, `Waived` or `Superseded`, and `validate.sh --strict` has no blocking errors.\n285:| Create spec folder | `./runtime/cli/spec/create.sh \"Description\" --short-name name --level 2` |\n288:| Track-root lists | `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/refresh-track-roots.mjs --apply` after moving, renaming or deleting a packet in a track by hand; `archive.sh` refreshes it itself. The pre-push hook blocks a commit whose track lists other packets than it holds |\n289:| Validate | `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh specs/007-feature/` |\n291:| Save context | `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js /tmp/save-context-data-<session-id>.json specs/007-feature/` |\n292:| Gate 1 trigger lookup | `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/lookup-trigger-index.mjs --json -- \"<prompt>\"` (exit `0` hit, `1` no-hit, `2` broken) |\n293:| Regenerate trigger index | `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/generate-trigger-index.mjs` |\n296:| Upgrade level | `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/upgrade-level.sh specs/007-feature/ --to 2` |\n297:| Completeness | `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh specs/007-feature/` |\n303:- `/deep:research` follows `../system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/spec-check-protocol.md` when research needs bounded `spec.md` anchoring.\n315:Then load task-specific resources from `references/`, templates from `assets/` and automation from `runtime/cli/` when present.\n317:Scripts: `runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh`, `runtime/cli/spec/create.sh`, `runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js`, `runtime/cli/spec/check-completion.sh`.\n319:Related skills: `sk-doc` for authored documentation quality, `sk-code` for code changes, `sk-git` for git handoff, and `system-deep-loop` for iterative research and audit (its `research` and `review` modes).\n"}
