{"type":"thinking","text":"Interesting: `runtime/cli/spec/README.md` line 120 DOES document exit 3 and rerun behavior, and phase 006-010 fixes (bare-name? pre-archive?). It was updated. The system-spec-kit README line 639 is thinner and does not mention exit codes. But is that stale? It says \"Dry run by default, --apply writes\" — no exit 3 claim, so omission rather than false. The review focus says \"docs stale against phases 006-010 behaviour, which SKILL.md, references, changelog, feature catalog, playbook and README were never updated for\". Maybe they mean not updated = missing coverage of new behaviors. Hmm.\n\nBut wait — the spec/README.md content includes phase 006-010 behavior: \"A rerun after status 3 finds nothing to do... rerunning a map that stopped part-way finishes it\", \"Preflight refuses ... a name that is not NNN-slug\", \"pre-archive\"? Let me check if it mentions bare-name/pre-archive rewrites. Line 120 mentions \"rewrites every whole old id under specs/\" — maybe stale re phase 007, because phase 007 added bare sibling names and pre-archive ids; \"every whole old id\" doesn't cover bare names. That could be a real doc gap: the README says \"rewrites every whole old id under specs/\" — after phase 007, it also rewrites bare sibling names in a phase parent and the pre-archive id. Let me verify what phase 007 changed in relocate.mjs and what the README says. This is a candidate P2/P1 doc finding.\n\nAlso archive.sh line 114 says \"When a live packet with another name already holds its number, the restore lands on the next free number above every live and archived packet there, through relocate.mjs\" — phase 008 changed the restore verdict to exit 3, mixed-track refusal. Does README mention mixed-track refusal on restore? It says \"A z_archive/ that is a symlink is refused on archive and on restore\" but not mixed-track refusal. Maybe missing. The doc line 114 is long and may have been updated? Let me check archive.sh behavior for mixed-track refusal and exit 3.\n\nLet me now read the docs that are likely stale:\n- feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-packet-relocation.md\n- manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-packet-relocation.md\n- feature-catalog spec-lifecycle-automation.md\n- sub-track-proposal.md\n- retrieval rg-archive-search.md\n- changelog v2.13.0.0.md\n- folder-structure.md / phase-definitions.md / quick-reference.md / worked-examples.md\n- SKILL.md (no relocate mention)\n- README root (manifest) — likely generic.\n\nLet me read the feature-catalog spec-packet-relocation and sub-track-proposal; these are most relevant."}
