{"type":"thinking","text":"The feature-catalog spec-packet-relocation.md is stale relative to phases 006-010:\n- Section 2 \"Refusals and exit codes\": line 66 says \"Status 2 means ... a failed close\" but phase 008 added exit 3 for a moved packet's validation failure after steps landed. It omits status 3 entirely. This is a concrete doc gap. The source code header lines 34-38 documents 3; the README line 120 documents 3. But the feature catalog line 66 says statuses 0/1/2 only and \"Status 2 means ... a failed close\" — actually if a moved packet's validation fails, the close validation failed but the run exits 3. So line 66's claim that status 2 covers \"a failed close\" is inaccurate for phase 008 behavior. P1? This is a doc/spec mismatch (traceability dimension) — probably P1 given the review focus and that feature catalog is supposed to be auditable. Reach: an operator reading the catalog expects exit 2 and treats exit 3 as unknown failure. That is a real reach. I'd call it P1 (spec mismatch) or P2. The review-core says P1 = \"correctness bug, spec mismatch, must-fix gate issue\"; P2 = \"documentation polish\". A false exit-code doc in the feature catalog seems spec mismatch (P1). But this is a documentation-only review; the consequences are misdiagnosis, not code failure. Hmm. Let me think about severity calibration later; maybe P1 for directly contradicted documented behavior, P2 for omitted new behavior. The review focus explicitly says \"Highest yield: docs stale...\" suggesting these are material. I'll likely assign P1 to direct contradictions (exit 3 omission in feature catalog/playbook where exit codes are enumerated), and P2 to omissions elsewhere.\n\n- Section 2 \"What a move rewrites\" line 44: \"An old id is matched as a whole path, so a longer id that starts with it is left alone.\" Doesn't mention bare sibling names in a phase parent's documents or pre-archive id rewriting. Phase 007 added these. So stale/incomplete. P1/P2.\n- Line 68: \"a run that stopped on a failed step is finished by running the same map again.\" This is fine but doesn't mention late-step ledger marks or exit 3 rerun; maybe okay.\n- Refusals list line 57-64 does not mention the case-folded duplicate refusal (phase 006). It says \"a source or destination named by two entries\" but not two case-foldings of one folder. Actually maybe \"two spellings of one folder\" — phase 006 preflight refuses two case spellings. Let me check relocate's preflight code for exact. Search for \"case\" / \"toLowerCase\" in relocate.mjs.\n- Line 33: renumber \"Numbers held in that folder's z_archive/ count as taken\" — phase 008 create.sh phase numbering reads z_archive; relocate renumber maybe already. Fine.\n- Line 47: step 6 \"moves are recorded in the relocation ledger, the citation redirect table is rebuilt and the trigger index is regenerated\" — then closes with sweep and validate. Phase 006 added late-step marks to resume; the catalog doesn't mention resume of redirect/trigger/sweep. It says line 68 \"a run that stopped on a failed step is finished by running the same map again\", which covers it partially but not the ledger marks.\n- Line 91: test coverage says relocate.vitest.ts covers repeated apply but not the new resume cases; phase 010 created relocate-real-pipeline.vitest.ts, not mentioned in the catalog at all. That's a stale source-files/test anchor. P2.\n\nPlaybook spec-packet-relocation.md:\n- Scenario doesn't cover exit 3/resume, bare-name/pre-archive rewrites, case-folded duplicates. Its title 492 and steps are old. Phase 006-010 changed behavior; playbook should include new scenarios? The operator focus says playbook never updated. The feature-catalog is supposed to match current state; the playbook is a manual test scenario, maybe not required to cover every new behavior but phase 006-010 added behavior that should be testable. The playbook's \"Pass/Fail\" line 227 mentions apply prints RESULT PASSED; if a moved packet fails validation, exit 3. Not covered. P2 or P1.\n\nLet me check the other docs: sub-track-proposal feature catalog/playbook (phase 009 changes), spec-lifecycle-automation (phase 008 restore verdict/mixed track), rg-archive-search (phase 009 archivedPaths), spec-validation-archive-reach playbook, changelog v2.13.0.0, folder-structure, phase-definitions, quick-reference, retrieval-conventions, search.md, command assets, system-spec-kit SKILL.md.\n\nLet me read those docs in batches. First feature-catalog sub-track-proposal and spec-lifecycle-automation, rg-archive-search."}
