{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-98777bf9cc8726d8","status":"completed","result":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/quick-reference.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n110: ### Start Here: Command Map\n111: \n112: If the runtime does not surface command menus clearly, use this compact command map first.\n113: \n114: **SpecKit workflow commands**\n115: - `/speckit:resume` - continue or recover existing spec-folder work\n116: - `/speckit:plan` - define or refine a scoped spec and plan\n117: - `/speckit:implement` - execute an existing spec and plan packet\n118: - `/speckit:complete` - run the full spec-to-implementation lifecycle\n119: \n120: **Deep-loop workflow commands**\n121: - `/deep:research` - run iterative research before planning\n122: - `/deep:review` - run iterative review and finding synthesis\n123: - `/deep:ai-council` - run multi-seat planning deliberation\n124: \n125: **Memory commands**\n126: - `/speckit:save` - write the current session context into the packet's continuity documents\n127: - `/speckit:search` - retrieve prior context, decisions, and analysis by ripgrep over spec and skill docs\n128: \n129: **Nested changelog generator (deprecated)**\n130: - Spec folders no longer get changelogs. Write new entries to `.skilled/changelog/` with `/create:changelog`.\n131: - `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/spec-folder/nested-changelog.js <spec-folder> --write` - re-render an existing packet changelog, with a deprecation notice on stderr. It refuses a packet that has no changelog and writes nothing\n132: \n133: ### Create Spec Folder\n134: \n135: Use `create.sh`. It numbers the packet from the highest number in use, and before it does, it lists the recent packets in the same track:\n136: \n137: ```bash\n138: bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/create.sh --track <track> --level <N> \"<short description>\"\n139: # In a declared sub-track, numbered from 001 inside it:\n140: bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/create.sh --track <track>/<sub> --level <N> \"<short description>\"\n141: ```\n142: \n143: ### Template Composition (Maintainer)\n144: \n145: ```bash\n146: # Render one or more manifest templates for inspection\n147: bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/templates/inline-gate-renderer.sh \\\n148:   --level 3 \\\n149:   --out-dir /tmp/spec-kit-render \\\n150:   .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/core/spec.md.tmpl \\\n151:   .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/core/plan.md.tmpl\n152: ```\n153: \n154: `create.sh --path` validates the resolved target before writing and rejects traversal outside the repository. Post-create validation is opt-in: set `SPECKIT_POST_VALIDATE=1` when CI or a strict local workflow should run `validate.sh --quiet` immediately after scaffolding.\n155: \n156: **Naming rules:**\n157: - 2-3 words (shorter is better)\n158: - Lowercase\n159: - Hyphen-separated\n160: - Action-noun structure\n161: \n162: **Good examples:** `fix-typo`, `add-auth`, `mcp-code-mode`, `cli-opencode`\n163: \n164: ### Manual Context Save\n165: \n166: Trigger manual context save:\n167: ```\n168: Say: \"save context\" or \"save conversation\"\n169: ```\n170: \n171: **Required Inputs:** Structured JSON is mandatory for routine saves, and the target spec folder is still required\n172: ```\n173: node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js /tmp/save-context-data-<session-id>.json specs/007-feature/\n174: ```\n175: \n176: Use `generate-context.js` for routine metadata saves. Quick direct edits are allowed only for `_memory.continuity` YAML frontmatter blocks in `implementation-summary.md`. There is no indexing hand-off after a save; regenerate `runtime/data/trigger-index.json` only when a document's `trigger_phrases` changed.\n177: \n178: ---\n179: \n180: ## 5. PRE-IMPLEMENTATION CHECKLIST (PROGRESSIVE ENHANCEMENT)\n181: \n182: Before making ANY file changes, verify:\n183: \n184: - [ ] Determined level (1/2/3/3+) or exempt (typo fix)\n185: - [ ] Created `/specs/[###-short-name]/`\n186: - [ ] Scaffolded ALL REQUIRED templates for chosen level:\n187:   - [ ] Level 1: spec.md + plan.md + tasks.md + implementation-summary.md\n188:   - [ ] Level 2: Level 1 + acceptance-criteria.md\n189:   - [ ] Level 3: Level 2 file set (decision-record.md on request)\n\n(Showing lines 110-189 of 747. Use offset=190 to continue.)\n</content>"}
