{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-95d8f2fb5435bbd7","status":"completed","result":"18:> Writing or amending a `goal.md`, including a phase parent's binding table? Use\n139:# In a declared sub-track, numbered from 001 inside it:\n227:| `draft` | Planning phase | 2 (can start) |\n231:| `archived` | Historical record | 5 (do not reuse) |\n251:✅ The work is a different change to the same artifact as an existing packet in the same track (a series parent, `phase-definitions.md` §2)\n253:The phased-packet preference does not override qualification. If only one or neither threshold is met and no series parent qualifies, continue or update a standard non-phased packet.\n263:New/unrelated work is allowed to use Option B, but the new packet must still be evaluated independently. If it meets both phase thresholds, create a new phased packet; otherwise create a standard packet.\n265:**Phased Packets:** If the target already has child phase folders, use the active child when the work fits that child's scope. For a distinct but related workstream, prefer Option C and add the next sequential child phase instead of creating a new top-level sibling packet. Use the coordination root only for phase-map updates, root-scope decisions, and tree-truth verification. Use Option B only when the work is outside the phase parent's documented purpose and scope.\n269:**Small-task definition:** \"Small\" means exempt work or work that remains Level 1 after LOC guidance and all secondary risk/complexity factors are applied. A Level 2 or Level 3 task that does not phase-qualify is not automatically \"small\"; it remains standard because the phase thresholds were not both met.\n277:- **Option A:** Continue in the detected/current spec or current phase child when its scope fits.\n278:- **Option B:** Create a new top-level packet for new/unrelated work; independently evaluate whether that new packet qualifies for phases.\n279:- **Option C:** Use another existing packet — a related spec when it is a better scope match, a specific child under an existing phase parent, a related standard packet decomposed into phases when it meets both phase thresholds, a sub-track of the track (an existing one, or a new one proposed as a whole-track map when the track's packets have grown into clusters), or a series parent when the work is a different change to the same artifact as an existing packet in the same track (phase-definitions.md §2).\n282:**Recommendation priority:** `C` for a distinct related workstream in an existing or qualifying phased packet, including a series parent; otherwise `A` when the current packet fits; otherwise `C` for another related packet or a sub-track of the track, existing or newly proposed; `B` only for new/unrelated work; `D` is never the default.\n494:**Phased Resume**: When the target folder has child phases, first resolve\n499:**Phase-Parent Resume Ladder**: When the resume target is a phase parent (folder has `[0-9]{3}-name/` children with `spec.md` or `description.json`), `/speckit:resume` honors the pointer first:\n507:- A save into a child points every phase-parent ancestor one level down toward it.\n508:- A save aimed at a phase parent moves the pointers only when a `--full-auto` save routes its continuity into a leaf, and otherwise moves none.\n511:- No `_memory.continuity` block exists at a phase parent (per the lean trio policy: parents have no `implementation-summary.md`).\n516:- No workspace-root fallback; direct CLI targets stay inside the selected root spec or phase packet\n538:| `/speckit:plan :with-phases` | Trigger phase decomposition as pre-workflow in plan or complete |\n539:| `create.sh --phase --phases N --phase-names a,b,c <description>` | Create a phase parent and named child phase folders |\n540:| `create.sh --phase --parent <parent> --phases N --phase-names a,b <description>` | Add named child phases to an existing parent spec |\n541:| `validate.sh <parent> --recursive` | Validate parent and all child phase folders |\n549:**Suggested phase counts:**\n550:- Score 25-34: 2 phases\n551:- Score 35-44: 3 phases\n552:- Score 45+: 4 phases\n559:├── 001-phase-one/    # Independent child spec folder\n560:├── 002-phase-two/\n561:└── 003-phase-three/\n569:**Full documentation:** See [phase-definitions.md](../structure/phase-definitions.md)\n622:1. LOAD the tasks.md verification region at completion phase\n"}
