{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-b40ee3f34fe72b9d","status":"completed","result":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/SKILL.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n275: \n276: ## 6. INTEGRATION POINTS\n277: \n278: P0 blocks, P1 requires completion or approved deferral, and P2 is optional. Code updates route through `sk-code`; documentation updates route through `sk-doc`; git handoff routes through `sk-git`.\n279: \n280: ### Quick Reference Commands\n281: \n282: | Command | Usage |\n283: | --- | --- |\n284: | Canonical intake | `/speckit:plan --intake-only \"Description\"` |\n285: | Create spec folder | `./runtime/cli/spec/create.sh \"Description\" --short-name name --level 2` |\n286: | Create in a track | Add `--track <track>` to the create command. The new packet is also listed in `specs/<track>/graph-metadata.json` |\n287: | Create in a sub-track | Add `--track <track>/<sub>` for a declared sub-track. Numbering restarts inside it, and `suggest-subtracks.mjs` names the best-fitting sub-track for a description |\n288: | Track-root lists | `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/refresh-track-roots.mjs --apply` after moving, renaming or deleting a packet in a track by hand; `archive.sh` refreshes it itself. The pre-push hook blocks a commit whose track lists other packets than it holds |\n289: | Validate | `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh specs/007-feature/` |\n290: | Verify code alignment drift | `python3 .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/assets/scripts/verify_alignment_drift.py --root .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit` |\n291: | Save context | `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js /tmp/save-context-data-<session-id>.json specs/007-feature/` |\n292: | Gate 1 trigger lookup | `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/lookup-trigger-index.mjs --json -- \"<prompt>\"` (exit `0` hit, `1` no-hit, `2` broken) |\n293: | Regenerate trigger index | `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/generate-trigger-index.mjs` |\n294: | Free-text retrieval | The ripgrep recipes in `references/retrieval/retrieval-conventions.md` §2, scoped by the trailing positional path |\n295: | Next spec number | `ls -d specs/[0-9]*/ \\| sed 's/.*\\/\\([0-9]*\\)-.*/\\1/' \\| sort -n \\| tail -1` |\n296: | Upgrade level | `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/upgrade-level.sh specs/007-feature/ --to 2` |\n297: | Completeness | `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh specs/007-feature/` |\n298: | Worktree isolation | `.skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh` creates a per-session git worktree with isolated `SPEC_KIT_DB_DIR` / `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR`. Pair with `worktree-reaper.sh` for teardown and `worktree-guard.sh` for lock enforcement |\n299: | Session cleanup | `.skilled/scripts/session-cleanup.sh` resolves PIDs across claude/opencode/opencode runtimes |\n300: \n301: Canonical command lifecycle:\n302: - `/speckit:plan --intake-only` establishes or repairs the packet when standalone intake is needed.\n303: - `/deep:research` follows `../system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/spec-check-protocol.md` when research needs bounded `spec.md` anchoring.\n304: - Either `/speckit:plan` or `/speckit:complete` continues from the same folder. It reuses the shared intake contract (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/intake-contract.md`) only when local `folder_state` still needs repair.\n305: - When intake runs, the returned `start_state` is the canonical downstream field.\n306: \n307: **Remember**: This skill is the foundational documentation orchestrator. It enforces structure, template usage, context preservation, and workflow-required validation for all file modifications. Every conversation that modifies files MUST have a spec folder.\n308: \n309: ---\n310: \n311: ## 7. REFERENCES AND RELATED RESOURCES\n312: \n313: The router discovers reference, asset and script docs dynamically.\n314: Start with these references: `references/workflows/quick-reference.md`, `references/templates/template-guide.md`, `references/validation/validation-rules.md`, `references/retrieval/retrieval-conventions.md`, `references/structure/grep-convention.md` and `references/memory/save-workflow.md`.\n315: Then load task-specific resources from `references/`, templates from `assets/` and automation from `runtime/cli/` when present.\n316: \n317: Scripts: `runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh`, `runtime/cli/spec/create.sh`, `runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js`, `runtime/cli/spec/check-completion.sh`.\n318: \n319: Related skills: `sk-doc` for authored documentation quality, `sk-code` for code changes, `sk-git` for git handoff, and `system-deep-loop` for iterative research and audit (its `research` and `review` modes).\n\n(End of file - total 319 lines)\n</content>"}
