{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-8a63675f29bf889a","status":"completed","result":"AGENTS.md:80:  - **C) Related** - Use another existing packet, a child of an existing phase parent, a related standard packet split into phases once it meets both thresholds independently, a sub-track of the track (an existing one, or a new one proposed as a whole-track map when the track's packets have grown into clusters), or a series parent for a different change to the same artifact as an existing same-track packet. **Reply with the folder or child path.**\nREADME.md:416:- **`relocate.mjs`** - move, renumber or re-parent spec packets and rewrite every store that records the path. Takes `--map <file.json>`, `--from` with `--to`, `--renumber <folder>` or `--declare-subtrack <track>/<name>`. Dry run by default, `--apply` writes\nREADME.md:417:- **`suggest-subtracks.mjs`** - propose a whole-track sub-track map for a flat track, or with `--describe` name the declared sub-track a new packet fits best. Writes nothing\nREADME.md:430:`--verbose` shows details behind each rule. `--recursive` validates a parent and all child phase folders. `--include-archive` works only with `--recursive` and also validates the packets in the `z_archive/` of the folder given and, for a track root, of each declared sub-track. `validate.sh` implements no rules itself. It hands every rule decision to a single Node orchestrator.\nREADME.md:478:  │  C) Related, a phase child, a sub-track     │\nREADME.md:709:      │                               │  live / stale / absent / archived\nREADME.md:1205:Two lexical lanes over spec docs and skill docs: trigger-index lookup with `--triggers`, which on a zero-hit also checks spec docs the index does not list yet, ripgrep recipes otherwise. `--paths` and `--count` pick the recipe, and `--packet <specFolder>` narrows the search roots. Archived packets are left out by default. `--include-archive` searches them as well through `rg-wrapper.mjs`, marks each archived path `[archived]` and lists the `description.json` and `graph-metadata.json` files of archived packets that hold the phrase. A phrase nobody wrote is a clean no-hit, never a nearest guess.\n"}
