{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-ba734565238915d0","status":"completed","result":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/.skilled/commands/speckit/search.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n100: | Evidence with surrounding lines, or anchor labelling | Section 2.4 | `--json -C 2` |\n101: \n102: Structured evidence, the default, runs through the wrapper. It composes the Section 2.1 recipe itself, keeps the first-ranked row per file and cuts at 20 files, so a common phrase cannot flood the answer:\n103: \n104: ```bash\n105: node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/rg-wrapper.mjs structured '<QUERY>' --json\n106: ```\n107: \n108: Narrow with one `--search-root <path>` per root in place of the default `specs .skilled`. Pass `--limit <n>` when the user asks for more files, and `--limit 0` for all of them. The record's `command` field is the exact `rg` line that ran. The wrapper reads a phrase that starts with `--` as a flag and exits `2`; run the raw Section 2.1 recipe for that phrase instead. The other three modes run their recipe directly.\n109: \n110: Archived packets are left out by default. Add `--include-archive` to any wrapper recipe to search them as well:\n111: \n112: ```bash\n113: node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/rg-wrapper.mjs path 'skill routing refactor' --include-archive\n114: ```\n115: \n116: A phrase that only an archived packet holds exits `1` without the flag and `0` with it, and each archived path ends `[archived]`. The flag drops the `!**/z_archive/**` glob from the recipe and marks every printed hit under a `z_archive` segment with `[archived]`. The JSON rows of the structured and count recipes carry `archived: true|false`. A second invocation then lists the `description.json` and `graph-metadata.json` files of archived packets that hold the phrase, under a `json    :` section, and the exit is `0` when either lane matches. The mode is opt-in only. `/speckit:resume` excludes archives and has no such flag, and the trigger-index lane never reads them.\n117: \n118: 1. Resolve the search roots. Narrow by path, never by pattern: `specs .skilled` for everything, `specs/<track>` for one track, `specs/<track>/<sub-track>` for one declared sub-track, `specs/<track>/<NNN-name>` for one packet, `specs/<track>/<sub-track>/<NNN-name>` for a packet inside a sub-track, `specs/<track>/<NNN-name>/<NNN-child-name>` for one phase child. `--packet <specFolder>` replaces the roots with that path.\n119: 2. Run exactly one recipe. Never combine `--json` with the path-only or count mode: ripgrep does not reject the combination, the last output-mode flag wins silently, and a JSONL parser handed count output sees an empty result rather than an error.\n120: 3. Branch on the exit status: `0` = matches, `1` = no match returned as an empty result, `2` or higher = an execution or configuration error.\n121: 4. Keep the wrapper's `results` in the order it returned them: it already applied the ranking tuple in `retrieval-conventions.md` Section 5 — evidence field, then normalized match class, then relative path and one-based line. Order raw-recipe output with the same tuple. Ripgrep supplies matches, paths and lines; it never ranks relevance, and no rendered output may imply that it does.\n122: 5. To label anchor evidence, search for the marker itself (`<!-- ANCHOR:id -->`) and treat a line inside a matched pair as anchor evidence. Report an unmatched or orphan marker as a diagnostic rather than dropping it.\n123: 6. Render with the Section 3 contract in the presentation asset.\n124: \n125: ### Unsupported requests\n126: \n127: The retired continuity database carried stateful capabilities that a read-only scan cannot provide. Each is a declared loss, not a degraded lane:\n128: \n129: - Semantic paraphrase, vector and BM25 fusion, decay, access tracking, session dedup.\n130: - Causal graph traversal, lineage and drift analysis (`causal`, `link`, `unlink`, `causal-stats`).\n131: - Epistemic baselines and learning history (`preflight`, `postflight`, `history`).\n132: - Channel ablations and eval dashboards (`ablation`, `dashboard`).\n133: \n134: Render the Section 6 unsupported notice from the presentation asset and stop. Do not substitute a keyword search for any of them and present it as the same answer.\n135: \n136: ---\n137: \n138: ## 5. PRESENTATION BOUNDARY\n139: \n140: The full presentation contract lives in `.skilled/commands/speckit/assets/search-presentation.txt`. This router may only inline the lane-selection rules and recipe mechanics above.\n141: \n142: The following content must come from the presentation asset, not from router prose:\n143: \n144: - Empty-argument startup question and targeted follow-up wording.\n\n(Showing lines 100-144 of 161. Use offset=145 to continue.)\n</content>"}
