ays create.sh creates phase folders, no numbering. So it's an omission, not a false statement. The focus says \"archive-aware phase numbering\" never updated. A doc gap: maybe the changelog line 141 \"create.sh reads the numbers in the target folder and in its z_archive/. With 001-a live and z_archive/007-b archived, the new packet is 008\" — this is about packets, not phases. Phase 008 extends it to phases; the changelog does not say phases. Still true for packets. The phase-definitions doc says \"add the next sequential child phase\" (quick-reference:265, phase-definitions:255). \"Sequential\" could imply above live and archived, but not explicit. I'd call this a P2 documentation gap at phase-definitions.md:255 and quick-reference:265. Evidence code: create.sh:1811-1828 (counts z_archive). Let me cite exact lines.\n\nSimilarly \"mixed-track restore refusal\": docs archive.sh README line 114 does not mention; feature catalog spec-lifecycle-automation (line 45) says \"A folder or link already at the exact restore path is refused\" and focuses on number; no mixed-track. The archive.sh help text (playbook line 212-230) also doesn't mention mixed-track refusal. The changelog (line 143-145) says restore onto number; no mixed-track. The phase 008 goal says \"A restore that refuses to put a flat packet beside sub-tracks.\" So docs stale: feature catalog line 45, runtime/cli/spec/README.md line 114, archive.sh help text, changelog Archives section. P1/P2.\n\n\"pre-archive id rewrite\": docs spec-packet-relocation.md line 44 and README.md:120 say \"rewrites every whole old id\" — the pre-archive id is not a \"whole old id\" of the destination, it's the source id without z_archive. The feature catalog's \"What a move rewrites\" step 3 says \"References to the old path are rewritten\" — arguably covers it (the old id before archive is the source id minus z_archive; not named). The review focus explicitly says this was never documented. Candidate finding: feature-catalog spec-packet-relocation.md:44 and runtime/cli/spec/README.md:120 describe only whole current ids and miss the pre-archive and bare-name rewrites. P2.\n\n\"case-folded duplicate refusal\": feature catalog refusals line 60 says \"a source or destination named by two entries\" — not \"two case spellings of one folder\". Code preflight uses foldCase. The docs' refusal list omits it. P2.\n\n\"phase-map bare-name and re-parent rewrites\": phase-definitions.md's phase map section (line 177-190) shows the map; no statement that relocate rewrites bare names. The phase 007 behavior is a tool behavior, so spec-packet-relocation.md is the natural place. README.md:120 says \"rewrites every whole old id under specs/\" — bare sibling names are not whole ids; so the README claim is incomplete but not false (it doesn't say \"only\"). Still, for a doc that enumerates what the run does, omission of two major rewrite classes is a gap. P2.\n\n\"reworded archive signal\": This is in graph-metadata.json (not in manifest). The manifest includes `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json`? No. Maybe the reworded signal in `graph-metadata.json` is excluded because generated JSON left out. But the review focus lists it. Which manifest file could contain it? `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/memory/trigger-config.md` maybe? Let me grep for \"find a phrase in archived spec packets\" across manifest files."}
