{"type":"thinking","text":"The graph-metadata.json (skill root, not in manifest) has line 109-111: \"validate the archived spec packets\", \"packets under z_archive\", \"quote a phrase in archived spec packets\". Phase 009 reworded the archive signal to avoid \"findings\". But graph-metadata.json is not in the manifest. The user's focus mentions \"reworded archive signal\" — perhaps the generated files are excluded from scope, and the check is whether docs were updated. We cannot review graph-metadata.json because it's out of manifest scope. But the focus says scope is exactly the manifest; we should note that the reworded signal lives in an excluded generated file and is therefore out of scope. Hmm. Wait, the manifest comment says \"generated JSON and fixtures left out\". graph-metadata.json is generated and excluded. So I can note in \"Ruled Out / Scope\" that the reworded archive signal's source (graph-metadata.json) is outside the manifest and cannot be verified as a doc gap; no manifest doc states the signal. That addresses it.\n\nNow let me check the manual-testing-playbook rg-archive-search and sub-track-proposal scenarios for stale claims. And the spec-validation-archive-reach playbook. Also feature-catalog track-root-children-lists and spec-validation-rule-engine. And feature-catalog.md root registration. Let me read a few targeted parts."}
