{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-9e69ac9fc643c8d7","status":"completed","result":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/retrieval/rg-archive-search.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"494 -- Ripgrep archive search\"\n3: description: \"This scenario validates archive-aware search for `494`. It focuses on rg-wrapper.mjs leaving archived packets out by default and, with --include-archive, marking each archived hit and listing matching archived metadata files.\"\n4: version: 1.0.0.0\n5: ---\n6: \n7: # 494 -- Ripgrep archive search\n8: \n9: This document captures the scratch-directory manual validation contract for `rg-wrapper.mjs --include-archive`.\n10: \n11: ---\n12: \n13: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n14: \n15: This scenario validates archive-aware search for `494`. It focuses on `rg-wrapper.mjs` leaving archived packets out by default and, with `--include-archive`, marking each archived hit and listing matching archived metadata files. The fixture lives in a scratch directory under the operating-system temp directory, and the wrapper searches it through `--root`. It never writes to this checkout.\n16: \n17: ### Why This Matters\n18: \n19: An archived packet is finished or abandoned work. Returned unmarked beside live packets it reads as current evidence. Left out with no way back in, it hides the history of a decision. The default search keeps the archive out, and the opt-in search says which hits are archived.\n20: \n21: ---\n22: \n23: ## 2. SCENARIO CONTRACT\n24: \n25: Operators run the exact prompt and command sequence for `494` and confirm each outcome without contradictory evidence.\n26: \n27: - Objective: Prove that the default recipes skip `z_archive/`, and that `--include-archive` adds the archived hit with an `[archived]` mark, an `archived` field on each JSON row and a `json    :` section naming the archived packet's matching `description.json`.\n28: - Real user request: `Search the specs for ledger reconciliation, and this time include archived packets. Tell me which hits are archived.`\n29: - Prompt: `Search the demo specs for \"ledger reconciliation\" with rg-wrapper.mjs, first without and then with --include-archive. Tell me which hits are archived. Return PASS or FAIL with the paths and the exit codes.`\n30: - Expected execution process: Build one live packet and one archived packet that both carry the phrase in a scratch directory, run the path recipe without the flag, then run the path, structured and count recipes with it.\n31: - Expected signals: Without the flag the path recipe reports `paths   : 1` and its command carries `--glob '!**/z_archive/**'`. With the flag it reports `paths   : 2`, the archived path ends in `[archived]`, the command no longer carries that glob, and a `json    : 1 archived metadata file(s)` section follows. The count recipe's JSON rows carry `\"archived\": false` for the live file and `\"archived\": true` for the archived one.\n32: - Desired user-visible outcome: A concise `PASS` that names the live hit and the archived hit apart, or a `FAIL` that names the first violated check.\n33: - Pass/fail: PASS if every condition in Section 3 Pass / Fail holds, FAIL if any one does not.\n34: \n35: ---\n36: \n37: ## 3. TEST EXECUTION\n38: \n39: ### Prompt\n40: \n41: ```text\n42: Search the demo specs for \"ledger reconciliation\" with rg-wrapper.mjs, first without and then with --include-archive. Tell me which hits are archived. Return PASS or FAIL with the paths and the exit codes.\n43: ```\n44: \n45: ### Commands\n46: \n47: 1. From the repository root, create an isolated scratch directory. Confirm the printed path begins with the operating-system temp directory and is not the repository root.\n48: \n49:    ```bash\n50:    export RG_ARCHIVE_DEMO=\"$(cd \"$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/rg-archive-manual.XXXXXX\")\" && pwd -P)\"\n51:    printf 'RG_ARCHIVE_DEMO=%s\\n' \"$RG_ARCHIVE_DEMO\"\n52:    ```\n53: \n54: 2. Build one live packet and one archived packet. Both carry the phrase in `spec.md`, and the archived packet also carries it in `description.json`.\n55: \n56:    ```bash\n57:    mkdir -p \"$RG_ARCHIVE_DEMO/specs/demo/001-alpha\" \"$RG_ARCHIVE_DEMO/specs/demo/z_archive/002-old\"\n58:    printf '# Alpha\\n\\nLedger reconciliation notes. Follow-up work lives in specs/demo/004-beta.\\n' > \"$RG_ARCHIVE_DEMO/specs/demo/001-alpha/spec.md\"\n59:    printf '# Old\\n\\nLedger reconciliation, first attempt.\\n' > \"$RG_ARCHIVE_DEMO/specs/demo/z_archive/002-old/spec.md\"\n60:    printf '{\"level\":\"task\",\"specFolder\":\"demo/z_archive/002-old\",\"description\":\"Ledger reconciliation, first attempt.\"}\\n' > \"$RG_ARCHIVE_DEMO/specs/demo/z_archive/002-old/description.json\"\n61:    ```\n62: \n63: 3. Run the path recipe without the flag.\n64: \n65:    ```bash\n66:    node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/rg-wrapper.mjs path \"ledger reconciliation\" --root \"$RG_ARCHIVE_DEMO\" --search-root specs\n67:    echo \"DEFAULT_EXIT=$?\"\n68:    ```\n69: \n70: 4. Run the path recipe with `--include-archive`.\n71: \n72:    ```bash\n73:    node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/rg-wrapper.mjs path \"ledger reconciliation\" --root \"$RG_ARCHIVE_DEMO\" --search-root specs --include-archive\n74:    echo \"ARCHIVE_PATH_EXIT=$?\"\n75:    ```\n76: \n77: 5. Run the structured recipe with `--include-archive`.\n78: \n79:    ```bash\n80:    node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/rg-wrapper.mjs structured \"ledger reconciliation\" --root \"$RG_ARCHIVE_DEMO\" --search-root specs --include-archive\n81:    echo \"ARCHIVE_STRUCTURED_EXIT=$?\"\n82:    ```\n83: \n84: 6. Run the count recipe with `--include-archive` and `--json`.\n85: \n86:    ```bash\n87:    node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/rg-wrapper.mjs count \"ledger reconciliation\" --root \"$RG_ARCHIVE_DEMO\" --search-root specs --include-archive --json\n88:    echo \"ARCHIVE_COUNT_EXIT=$?\"\n89:    ```\n90: \n91: 7. Remove the scratch directory.\n92: \n93:    ```bash\n94:    rm -rf \"$RG_ARCHIVE_DEMO\"\n95:    ```\n96: \n97: ### Expected\n98: \n99: Step 3 prints the live packet only and `DEFAULT_EXIT=0`.\n100: \n101: ```text\n102: recipe  : path\n103: command : rg --no-config --hidden --fixed-strings --ignore-case --files-with-matches --max-count 1 --glob '*.md' --glob '!**/z_archive/**' --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/.git/**' --glob '!**/scratch/**' -- 'ledger reconciliation' specs\n104: exit    : 0 (match)\n105: paths   : 1\n106:   specs/demo/001-alpha/spec.md\n107: ```\n108: \n109: Step 4 prints both packets, marks the archived one, lists the archived metadata file and prints `ARCHIVE_PATH_EXIT=0`.\n110: \n111: ```text\n112: recipe  : path\n113: command : rg --no-config --hidden --fixed-strings --ignore-case --files-with-matches --max-count 1 --glob '*.md' --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/.git/**' --glob '!**/scratch/**' -- 'ledger reconciliation' specs\n114: exit    : 0 (match)\n115: paths   : 2\n116:   specs/demo/001-alpha/spec.md\n117:   specs/demo/z_archive/002-old/spec.md  [archived]\n118: json    : 1 archived metadata file(s)\n119:   specs/demo/z_archive/002-old/description.json  [archived]\n120: ```\n121: \n122: Step 5 prints one ranked row per file with the same mark and `ARCHIVE_STRUCTURED_EXIT=0`.\n123: \n124: ```text\n125: recipe  : structured\n126: command : rg --no-config --hidden --json --fixed-strings --ignore-case --glob '*.md' --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/.git/**' --glob '!**/scratch/**' -- 'ledger reconciliation' specs\n127: exit    : 0 (match)\n128: ranked  : 2 match(es) in 2 file(s); showing 2 file(s) at limit 20\n129:   body                 specs/demo/001-alpha/spec.md:3\n130:   body                 specs/demo/z_archive/002-old/spec.md:3  [archived]\n131: json    : 1 archived metadata file(s)\n132:   specs/demo/z_archive/002-old/description.json  [archived]\n133: ```\n134: \n135: Step 6 prints one JSON record and `ARCHIVE_COUNT_EXIT=0`. The record carries these fields among others.\n136: \n137: ```json\n138: {\n139:   \"counts\": [\n140:     {\n141:       \"archived\": false,\n142:       \"count\": 1,\n143:       \"path\": \"specs/demo/001-alpha/spec.md\"\n144:     },\n145:     {\n146:       \"archived\": true,\n147:       \"count\": 1,\n148:       \"path\": \"specs/demo/z_archive/002-old/spec.md\"\n149:     }\n150:   ],\n151:   \"exitCode\": 0,\n152:   \"fileCount\": 2,\n153:   \"inclu","truncated":true}
{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-84d64a4ae3e082fc","status":"completed","result":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/sub-track-proposal.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"493 -- Sub-track proposal\"\n3: description: \"This scenario validates the sub-track proposal for `493`. It focuses on suggest-subtracks.mjs printing a whole-track map for a flat track, withholding it below the threshold and writing nothing.\"\n4: version: 1.0.0.0\n5: ---\n6: \n7: # 493 -- Sub-track proposal\n8: \n9: This document captures the scratch-directory manual validation contract for `suggest-subtracks.mjs`.\n10: \n11: ---\n12: \n13: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n14: \n15: This scenario validates the sub-track proposal for `493`. It focuses on `suggest-subtracks.mjs` printing a whole-track map for a flat track, withholding it below the threshold and writing nothing. The fixture track lives in a scratch directory under the operating-system temp directory, and the tool reads it through `--specs`. It never reads or writes this checkout's `specs/` tree.\n16: \n17: ### Why This Matters\n18: \n19: A track that grows flat mixes unrelated subjects in one list. The proposal groups packets by the words their `description.json` keywords and graph metadata already carry, and prints the grouping as a `from` and `to` map. It is advice. Nothing moves until an operator reviews the map and hands it to `relocate.mjs --map`.\n20: \n21: ---\n22: \n23: ## 2. SCENARIO CONTRACT\n24: \n25: Operators run the exact prompt and command sequence for `493` and confirm each outcome without contradictory evidence.\n26: \n27: - Objective: Prove that `suggest-subtracks.mjs` withholds a map below its threshold, prints a map covering every packet once the threshold is met, answers a `--describe` question on a flat track with a plain sentence, rejects a track that does not exist and leaves the fixture unchanged.\n28: - Real user request: `The tools track is one flat list. Suggest how its packets could be grouped into sub-tracks, but don't move anything yet.`\n29: - Prompt: `Propose a sub-track grouping for the flat tools track with suggest-subtracks.mjs and show me the map it prints. Do not move or write anything. Return PASS or FAIL with the map and the exit codes.`\n30: - Expected execution process: Build a five-packet `tools` track in a scratch directory, run the proposal at the default threshold, rerun it with `--threshold 4`, ask a `--describe` question, name a missing track and list the fixture.\n31: - Expected signals: The default run prints `track tools has 5 live packets, below the threshold of 8; no map`. The `--threshold 4` run prints a JSON array of five `from` and `to` pairs on stdout and three group lines on stderr. The `--describe` run prints `track tools is flat; no sub-track to fit`. The missing track exits `2`. The fixture listing is unchanged.\n32: - Desired user-visible outcome: A concise `PASS` with the proposed map and the exit codes, or a `FAIL` that names the first violated check.\n33: - Pass/fail: PASS if every condition in Section 3 Pass / Fail holds, FAIL if any one does not.\n34: \n35: ---\n36: \n37: ## 3. TEST EXECUTION\n38: \n39: ### Prompt\n40: \n41: ```text\n42: Propose a sub-track grouping for the flat tools track with suggest-subtracks.mjs and show me the map it prints. Do not move or write anything. Return PASS or FAIL with the map and the exit codes.\n43: ```\n44: \n45: ### Commands\n46: \n47: 1. From the repository root, create an isolated scratch directory. Confirm the printed path begins with the operating-system temp directory and is not the repository root.\n48: \n49:    ```bash\n50:    export SUBTRACK_DEMO=\"$(cd \"$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/subtrack-manual.XXXXXX\")\" && pwd -P)\"\n51:    printf 'SUBTRACK_DEMO=%s\\n' \"$SUBTRACK_DEMO\"\n52:    ```\n53: \n54: 2. Build a flat `tools` track with five packets. Two share ranking words, two share archive words and one shares nothing.\n55: \n56:    ```bash\n57:    mkdir -p \"$SUBTRACK_DEMO/specs/tools/001-rank-tuning\" \"$SUBTRACK_DEMO/specs/tools/002-rank-cache\" \"$SUBTRACK_DEMO/specs/tools/003-archive-restore\" \"$SUBTRACK_DEMO/specs/tools/004-archive-listing\" \"$SUBTRACK_DEMO/specs/tools/005-release-notes\"\n58:    printf '# Rank tuning\\n' > \"$SUBTRACK_DEMO/specs/tools/001-rank-tuning/spec.md\"\n59:    printf '# Rank cache\\n' > \"$SUBTRACK_DEMO/specs/tools/002-rank-cache/spec.md\"\n60:    printf '# Archive restore\\n' > \"$SUBTRACK_DEMO/specs/tools/003-archive-restore/spec.md\"\n61:    printf '# Archive listing\\n' > \"$SUBTRACK_DEMO/specs/tools/004-archive-listing/spec.md\"\n62:    printf '# Release notes\\n' > \"$SUBTRACK_DEMO/specs/tools/005-release-notes/spec.md\"\n63:    printf '{\"level\":\"task\",\"specFolder\":\"tools/001-rank-tuning\",\"keywords\":[\"search ranking\",\"ranking weights\"]}\\n' > \"$SUBTRACK_DEMO/specs/tools/001-rank-tuning/description.json\"\n64:    printf '{\"level\":\"task\",\"specFolder\":\"tools/002-rank-cache\",\"keywords\":[\"search ranking\",\"ranking cache\"]}\\n' > \"$SUBTRACK_DEMO/specs/tools/002-rank-cache/description.json\"\n65:    printf '{\"level\":\"task\",\"specFolder\":\"tools/003-archive-restore\",\"keywords\":[\"archive restore\",\"restore numbering\"]}\\n' > \"$SUBTRACK_DEMO/specs/tools/003-archive-restore/description.json\"\n66:    printf '{\"level\":\"task\",\"specFolder\":\"tools/004-archive-listing\",\"keywords\":[\"archive restore\",\"archive listing\"]}\\n' > \"$SUBTRACK_DEMO/specs/tools/004-archive-listing/description.json\"\n67:    printf '{\"level\":\"task\",\"specFolder\":\"tools/005-release-notes\",\"keywords\":[\"release notes\"]}\\n' > \"$SUBTRACK_DEMO/specs/tools/005-release-notes/description.json\"\n68:    ```\n69: \n70: 3. Run the proposal at the default threshold of 8.\n71: \n72:    ```bash\n73:    node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/suggest-subtracks.mjs --track tools --specs \"$SUBTRACK_DEMO/specs\"\n74:    echo \"DEFAULT_EXIT=$?\"\n75:    ```\n76: \n77: 4. Lower the threshold so the five packets qualify.\n78: \n79:    ```bash\n80:    node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/suggest-subtracks.mjs --track tools --specs \"$SUBTRACK_DEMO/specs\" --threshold 4\n81:    echo \"MAP_EXIT=$?\"\n82:    ```\n83: \n84: 5. Ask which declared sub-track a new packet fits. The track is flat, so there is none to fit.\n85: \n86:    ```bash\n87:    node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/suggest-subtracks.mjs --track tools --specs \"$SUBTRACK_DEMO/specs\" --describe \"archive restore numbering\"\n88:    echo \"DESCRIBE_EXIT=$?\"\n89:    ```\n90: \n91: 6. Name a track that does not exist, then list the fixture to confirm nothing was created or moved.\n92: \n93:    ```bash\n94:    node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/suggest-subtracks.mjs --track missing --specs \"$SUBTRACK_DEMO/specs\"\n95:    echo \"MISSING_EXIT=$?\"\n96:    ls \"$SUBTRACK_DEMO/specs/tools\"\n97:    ```\n98: \n99: 7. Remove the scratch directory.\n100: \n101:    ```bash\n102:    rm -rf \"$SUBTRACK_DEMO\"\n103:    ```\n104: \n105: ### Expected\n106: \n107: Step 3 prints one line and `DEFAULT_EXIT=0`.\n108: \n109: ```text\n110: track tools has 5 live packets, below the threshold of 8; no map\n111: ```\n112: \n113: Step 4 prints three group lines on stderr, the map on stdout and `MAP_EXIT=0`. Each packet is renumbered from `001` inside its proposed sub-track, and the packet that shares no words lands in `general`.\n114: \n115: ```text\n116: suggest-subtracks: tools/ranking-search <- 001-rank-tuning, 002-rank-cache\n117: suggest-subtracks: tools/archive-restore <- 003-archive-restore, 004-archive-listing\n118: suggest-subtracks: tools/general <- 005-release-notes\n119: [\n120:   {\n121:     \"from\": \"tools/001-rank-tuning\",\n122:     \"to\": \"tools/ranking-search/001-rank-tuning\"\n123:   },\n124:   {\n125:     \"from\": \"tools/002-rank-cache\",\n126:     \"to\": \"tools/ranking-search/002-rank-cache\"\n127:   },\n128:   {\n129:     \"from\": \"tools/003-archive-restore\",\n130:     \"to\": \"tools/archive-restore/001-archive-restore\"\n131:   },\n132:   {\n133:     \"from\": \"tools/004-archive-listing\",\n134:     \"to\": \"tools/archive-restore/002-archive-listing\"\n135:   },\n136:   {\n137:     \"from\": \"tools/005-release-notes\",\n138:     \"to\": \"tools/general/001-release-notes\"\n139:   }\n140: ]\n141: ```\n142: \n143: Step 5 prints one line and `DESCRIBE_EXIT=0`.\n144: \n145: ```text\n146: track tools is flat; no ","truncated":true}
