{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-b3f7ca81a96a3fa5","status":"completed","result":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-validation-archive-reach.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"495 -- Spec validation of archived packets\"\n3: description: \"This scenario validates archive-aware validation for `495`. It focuses on validate.sh --recursive visiting an archived packet only when --include-archive is passed, and refusing that flag without --recursive.\"\n4: version: 1.0.0.0\n5: ---\n6: \n7: # 495 -- Spec validation of archived packets\n8: \n9: This document captures the scratch-directory manual validation contract for `validate.sh --recursive --include-archive`.\n10: \n11: ---\n12: \n13: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n14: \n15: This scenario validates archive-aware validation for `495`. It focuses on `validate.sh --recursive` visiting an archived packet only when `--include-archive` is passed, and refusing that flag without `--recursive`. The fixture track lives in a scratch directory under the operating-system temp directory. The scenario never validates or writes this checkout's `specs/` tree.\n16: \n17: ### Why This Matters\n18: \n19: A recursive run walks a track's live packets and stops at `z_archive/`. That keeps a normal gate fast and free of old findings, but it also means nothing checks an archived packet after a move or a restore. The flag adds the packets in the `z_archive/` of the folder given and, for a track root, of each declared sub-track.\n20: \n21: ---\n22: \n23: ## 2. SCENARIO CONTRACT\n24: \n25: Operators run the exact prompt and command sequence for `495` and confirm each outcome without contradictory evidence.\n26: \n27: - Objective: Prove that a recursive validation of a track reports its live packets only, that the same run with `--include-archive` also reports the archived packet, and that `--include-archive` without `--recursive` is refused with exit `2`.\n28: - Real user request: `Validate the demo track again, and this time include the archived packets. Show me which folders were checked.`\n29: - Prompt: `Validate the demo track with validate.sh --recursive, first without and then with --include-archive, and list the folders each run checked. Confirm the flag is refused without --recursive. Return PASS or FAIL with the folder lists and the exit codes.`\n30: - Expected execution process: Build a track with three live packets and one archived packet in a scratch directory, list the `Folder:` lines of a recursive run, repeat with `--include-archive`, then pass the flag alone.\n31: - Expected signals: The recursive run prints four `Folder:` lines, the track and its three live packets. The archive run prints five, the fifth ending in `specs/demo/z_archive/002-old`. The flag alone prints `ERROR: --include-archive requires --recursive` and exits `2`.\n32: - Desired user-visible outcome: A concise `PASS` with both folder lists, or a `FAIL` that names the first violated check.\n33: - Pass/fail: PASS if every condition in Section 3 Pass / Fail holds, FAIL if any one does not.\n34: \n35: ---\n36: \n37: ## 3. TEST EXECUTION\n38: \n39: ### Prompt\n40: \n41: ```text\n42: Validate the demo track with validate.sh --recursive, first without and then with --include-archive, and list the folders each run checked. Confirm the flag is refused without --recursive. Return PASS or FAIL with the folder lists and the exit codes.\n43: ```\n44: \n45: ### Commands\n46: \n47: 1. From the repository root, create an isolated scratch directory. Confirm the printed path begins with the operating-system temp directory and is not the repository root.\n48: \n49:    ```bash\n50:    export VALIDATE_ARCHIVE_DEMO=\"$(cd \"$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/validate-archive-manual.XXXXXX\")\" && pwd -P)\"\n51:    printf 'VALIDATE_ARCHIVE_DEMO=%s\\n' \"$VALIDATE_ARCHIVE_DEMO\"\n52:    ```\n53: \n54: 2. Build a `demo` track with three live packets and one archived packet. Each packet holds a bare `spec.md` and its two metadata files.\n55: \n56:    ```bash\n57:    cd \"$VALIDATE_ARCHIVE_DEMO\"\n58:    mkdir -p specs/demo/001-alpha specs/demo/004-beta specs/demo/006-gamma specs/demo/z_archive/002-old\n59:    printf '{\"level\":\"track\",\"specFolder\":\"demo\",\"description\":\"Fixture track.\"}\\n' > specs/demo/description.json\n60:    printf '{\"schema_version\":1,\"packet_id\":\"demo\",\"spec_folder\":\"demo\",\"parent_id\":null,\"children_ids\":[\"demo/001-alpha\",\"demo/004-beta\",\"demo/006-gamma\"]}\\n' > specs/demo/graph-metadata.json\n61:    printf '# Alpha\\n\\nLedger reconciliation notes. Follow-up work lives in specs/demo/004-beta.\\n' > specs/demo/001-alpha/spec.md\n62:    printf '# Beta\\n' > specs/demo/004-beta/spec.md\n63:    printf '# Gamma\\n' > specs/demo/006-gamma/spec.md\n64:    printf '# Old\\n\\nLedger reconciliation, first attempt.\\n' > specs/demo/z_archive/002-old/spec.md\n65:    printf '{\"level\":\"task\",\"specFolder\":\"demo/001-alpha\",\"description\":\"Fixture packet.\"}\\n' > specs/demo/001-alpha/description.json\n66:    printf '{\"level\":\"task\",\"specFolder\":\"demo/004-beta\",\"description\":\"Fixture packet.\"}\\n' > specs/demo/004-beta/description.json\n67:    printf '{\"level\":\"task\",\"specFolder\":\"demo/006-gamma\",\"description\":\"Fixture packet.\"}\\n' > specs/demo/006-gamma/description.json\n68:    printf '{\"level\":\"task\",\"specFolder\":\"demo/z_archive/002-old\",\"description\":\"Ledger reconciliation, first attempt.\"}\\n' > specs/demo/z_archive/002-old/description.json\n69:    printf '{\"schema_version\":1,\"packet_id\":\"demo/001-alpha\",\"spec_folder\":\"demo/001-alpha\",\"parent_id\":\"demo\",\"children_ids\":[]}\\n' > specs/demo/001-alpha/graph-metadata.json\n70:    printf '{\"schema_version\":1,\"packet_id\":\"demo/004-beta\",\"spec_folder\":\"demo/004-beta\",\"parent_id\":\"demo\",\"children_ids\":[]}\\n' > specs/demo/004-beta/graph-metadata.json\n71:    printf '{\"schema_version\":1,\"packet_id\":\"demo/006-gamma\",\"spec_folder\":\"demo/006-gamma\",\"parent_id\":\"demo\",\"children_ids\":[]}\\n' > specs/demo/006-gamma/graph-metadata.json\n72:    printf '{\"schema_version\":1,\"packet_id\":\"demo/z_archive/002-old\",\"spec_folder\":\"demo/z_archive/002-old\",\"parent_id\":\"demo\",\"children_ids\":[]}\\n' > specs/demo/z_archive/002-old/graph-metadata.json\n73:    cd -\n74:    ```\n75: \n76: 3. From the repository root, validate the track recursively and keep the folder lines.\n77: \n78:    ```bash\n79:    bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh \"$VALIDATE_ARCHIVE_DEMO/specs/demo\" --recursive 2>&1 | grep \"Folder:\"\n80:    ```\n81: \n82: 4. Repeat with `--include-archive`.\n83: \n84:    ```bash\n85:    bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh \"$VALIDATE_ARCHIVE_DEMO/specs/demo\" --recursive --include-archive 2>&1 | grep \"Folder:\"\n86:    ```\n87: \n88: 5. Print one result line per folder for both runs, with each run's exit status.\n89: \n90:    ```bash\n91:    bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh \"$VALIDATE_ARCHIVE_DEMO/specs/demo\" --recursive --quiet\n92:    echo \"RECURSIVE_EXIT=$?\"\n93:    bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh \"$VALIDATE_ARCHIVE_DEMO/specs/demo\" --recursive --include-archive --quiet\n94:    echo \"ARCHIVE_EXIT=$?\"\n95:    ```\n96: \n97: 6. Pass the flag without `--recursive`.\n98: \n99:    ```bash\n100:    bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh \"$VALIDATE_ARCHIVE_DEMO/specs/demo\" --include-archive\n101:    echo \"FLAG_ALONE_EXIT=$?\"\n102:    ```\n103: \n104: 7. Remove the scratch directory.\n105: \n106:    ```bash\n107:    rm -rf \"$VALIDATE_ARCHIVE_DEMO\"\n108:    ```\n109: \n110: ### Expected\n111: \n112: Step 3 prints four lines. `<demo>` stands for the printed `VALIDATE_ARCHIVE_DEMO` path.\n113: \n114: ```text\n115:   Folder: <demo>/specs/demo\n116:   Folder: <demo>/specs/demo/001-alpha\n117:   Folder: <demo>/specs/demo/004-beta\n118:   Folder: <demo>/specs/demo/006-gamma\n119: ```\n120: \n\n(Showing lines 1-120 of 198. Use offset=121 to continue.)\n</content>"}
