and the real pipeline suite exits 1 against the migrate mutant. 7: see validation |\n139:| Criteria 2 and 3 rerun on the final tree 2026-11-14 | Done | The earlier criteria row leaned on tests for 2 and 3, so both were rerun literally in a throwaway clone of `96ea4dc02a` with its own runtime build. 2: a 10-packet track `clus` with a track root, `suggest-subtracks.mjs --track clus` exit 0 with a 10-entry map in two groups, `relocate.mjs --map` dry run exit 1 with `moves=10 moved=0 rewrites=21 identity=10 roots=3 ledger=10` and no refusal, `git status --porcelain` empty before and after. 3: with `specs/demo/001-a` live and `z_archive/007-b` archived by `archive.sh`, `create.sh --track demo --skip-branch` exit 0 created `008-next-one`. With `002-gamma` archived from a two-phase parent, `create.sh --phase --parent` created `003-delta` with Predecessor `001-alpha`. Clone deleted afterwards |\n140:| Docs written by the orchestrator | Deviation | The claude2 account hit its usage limit. The operator chose that this session writes the phase docs from the saved build evidence |\n153:| Open question: fixture for the proposal check | Phase 005 AC-008 and completion criterion 2 name a real flat track with more than eight packets. None exists, and the largest holds 6. The check passed on a 10-packet fixture track in a clone. Does the operator accept the fixture through a decision record? |\n154:| Amendment 2026-11-14: decision D5 | D5 said the work runs as five phases. It now names phases 006 to 010 and the findings they close, reviewer A 1 to 12 and reviewer B 6 to 8, on operator decision Q010 in `decision-record.md`. |\n156:| Amendment 2026-11-14: criteria folded to seven | Each remediation criterion joined the existing criterion on its surface, and the routing check lives in the 009 child goal. Each phase stays observable: 006 in the first criterion, 008 in the third, 009 in the fourth, 007 in the fifth and 010 in the sixth. The fold answers the earlier open question on the c