{"type":"thinking","text":"Decision record confirms:\n- \"Not planned: renumber resume\" — so changelog line 221 is accurate. Good.\n- Residual against D3: phase column number etc. keep old number — out of scope. This is a known decision; don't report as finding (or note in ruled out).\n- \"Docs written by the orchestrator\" etc.\n\nThe review focus: docs stale against 006-010. Could there be an explicit requirement that docs be updated? The phases 006-010 scope boundaries don't mention docs. The parent spec's \"Files to Change\" table lists docs modified for phases 001-005 but not 006-010 doc updates. So the packet never planned doc updates for 006-010. The operator's review focus is precisely to identify that gap. Findings are still valid as documentation traceability issues against the skill standards (shipped behavior must be documented with source anchors; feature catalog current-state). The feature catalog standard requires each per-feature file to document shipped behavior. Stale docs violate that.\n\nNow let me check whether the `feature-catalog.md` root registers the new features with statuses/versions; likely okay.\n\nI need to move to writing iteration 1. But first, gather enough evidence for each planned finding. Let me define the findings set (draft):\n\nF1 (P1, traceability): `SKILL.md:295` \"Next spec number\" command counts only live root folders, contradicting D4 and create.sh archive-aware numbering. Following it can reuse an archived number. Evidence code: create.sh:1638-1661 (root/track/sub-track numbering includes z_archive), phase 008: create.sh:1811-1828 for phases. Doc scope: SKILL.md. Fix: add z_archive to the one-liner or point to create.sh.\n\nF2 (P1, traceability): `feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-packet-relocation.md:66` exit status enumerates 0/1/2 and omits 3, so a validation-only failure after landing steps is documented as status 2/none. Evidence: relocate.mjs:34-38, closeRun at ~1640-1660 returns 3 (need exact line). Let me