{"type":"thinking","text":"Note: closeRun returns 3 only if status === 0 when the validation fails; if the sweep failed status=2, validation failure doesn't change it. So exit 3 means sweep passed and only packet validation failed. Matches header.\n\nF3 (P1, traceability): `feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:45` says a failed relocate run makes restore exit 1; phase 008 makes status 3 a success-with-warning (archive.sh:437-440). Also omits mixed-track refusal (archive.sh:363-395). Could be one finding with both gaps or two. I'll make it one finding \"restore section predates phase 008\" citing line 45, with both behaviors; the case is a restore whose relocated packet fails its own validation → catalog says exit 1 but code exits 0; and a flat restore into a sub-tracked track → catalog says nothing though code refuses. P1 because a documented exit status is contradicted.\n\nF4 (P1, traceability): `feature-catalog/retrieval/rg-archive-search.md:28` says path-only JSON stays plain strings and never mentions `archivedPaths`; phase 009 adds it. The parent goal's completion criterion 4 requires the path record to mark archived paths. P1/P2. It's a current-state catalog that fails to document a shipped field. I'd call P1 because the field is the point of the phase and a JSON consumer can't know. But is it \"must-fix gate issue\"? The phase's acceptance criterion is met in code; docs lag. In this review, doc correctness is the product. I'll rate P1.\n\nF5 (P1, traceability): `references/structure/folder-structure.md:141` enumerates exactly three \"no map\" cases, omitting the phase 009 non-NNN-slug refusal (suggest-subtracks.mjs:293-299) and does not say proposed names avoid existing undeclared folders (suggest-subtracks.mjs:153-155, 254). The three-case claim is now false: there is a fourth case. P1? It's a direct false count in reference doc. Could be P1 since it's a spec mismatch; but impact is low (operator expects a grouping and gets a refusal line). I'd rate P2 maybe. Hmm. Review-core: P2 = documentation polish. A false \"three cases\" statement in a structure reference is a documentation correctness issue but low impact. I'll make it P2.\n\nF6 (P1, traceability): `feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-packet-relocation.md:44` says \"An old id is matched as a whole path...\" and doesn't document the bare sibling-name rewrite or pre-archive id rewrite (relocate.mjs:651-654, bareNameEdits/phaseRowEdits at 1363). The current-state catalog's \"What a move rewrites\" is incomplete for two phase 007 behaviors. Is this P1 or P2? The doc is not false, just incomplete. P2.\n\nF7 (P2): `feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-packet-relocation.md:60` refusal list omits the case-folded duplicate refusal (relocate.mjs:472-490). The doc says \"a source or destination named by two entries\" but not two case spellings. P2.\n\nF8 (P2): `changelog/v2.13.0.0.md:67` exit codes omit 3. Since it's a historical release note, P2. But wait — if the changelog is not updated for 006-010, then it's stale. The operator focus lists it. P1? I'd rather not double-report exit 3: F2 is the current-state catalog (P1); F8 is the release note (P2) with the same root cause. Maybe combine? The finding schema allows affectedSurfaceHints; but exact file:line per gap is requested. I'll make F8 a separate P2: \"changelog release note never updated for 006-010 behavior\" listing exit 3 and archivedPaths etc. Hmm, that's a broad finding. Better: one P2 finding for changelog:67 exit codes, one P2 for changelog:165 archived JSON omitted? That's a lot.\n\nLet me think about the ideal output for the operator: a concise set of findings that maps each undocumented phase 006-010 behavior to its doc lines, plus clean docs. Maybe 10-12 findings:\n\n1. P1 SKILL.md:295 next-number command ignores z_archive (D4 violation).\n2. P1 feature-catalog spec-packet-relocation.md:66 exit 3 missing.\n3. P1 feature-catalog spec-lifecycle-automation.md:45 restore exit-3 verdict + mixed-track refusal missing.\n4. P1 feature-catalog rg-archive-search.md:28 archivedPaths missing.\n5. P2 folder-structure.md:141 \"three cases\" omits non-NNN-slug refusal; group names avoid existing folders unstated.\n6. P2 feature-catalog spec-packet-relocation.md:44 bare-name/pre-archive rewrites missing.\n7. P2 feature-catalog spec-packet-relocation.md:60 case-folded duplicate refusal missing.\n8. P2 changelog:67 exit 3 missing; changelog:165 archivedPaths missing (maybe combine into one changelog finding at line 67, with affected surfaces).\n9. P2 SKILL.md:317 script list omits relocate/suggest/archive; SKILL.md quick reference has no relocate/archive rows (discoverability).\n10. P2 playbook spec-packet-relocation.md:226 pass/fail only expects exit 0, no exit 3/resume case.\n11. P2 playbook rg-archive-search.md:176 pass/fail doesn't check archivedPaths in path JSON.\n12. P2 playbook sub-track-proposal.md:169 pass/fail doesn't feed map to relocate preflight (phase 009 guarantee).\n12b. P2 playbook 495? No phase 006-010 changes to validation.\n13. P2 phase-definitions.md:255 / quick-reference:265 phase numbering doesn't state archived phases count.\n14. P2 README (system-spec-kit):639 relocate row omits exit 3/resume details? But spec/README.md:120 is detailed; the system README is an index/table; maybe no change needed. Or P2 that system README's archive row omits mixed-track refusal/exit 3. Hmm.\n\nAnd clean docs:\n- `runtime/cli/spec/README.md:120` already documents exit 3, resume, preflight NNN-slug, ledger; line 114 covers restore next-number but not mixed-track; maybe not fully clean.\n- `.skilled/commands/speckit/search.md:116` mentions archived rows but not archivedPaths; not clean.\n- root README.md lines 416-417, 430: high-level; no change needed for exit codes (it's a summary).\n- AGENTS.md:80 option C includes sub-track; no phase 006-010 behavior is relevant; no change needed.\n- references/retrieval-conventions.md:84: mentions archived rows; no archivedPaths; gap.\n- `.skilled/commands/speckit/search.md:116` and search-presentation.txt:120/127/128: no archivedPaths. Gap.\nSo the \"docs need no change\" list: root `README.md` (feature roundup already names the tools; no exit-code contract), `AGENTS.md` (option C already correct), `references/structure/phase-definitions.md`? no, phase numbering gap. `references/workflows/worked-examples.md` (only option C wording, correct). `changelog`? no. `feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/track-root-children-lists.md`? Need to check. `spec-validation-rule-engine.md`? aligned. `manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-validation-archive-reach.md`? aligned (phase 004). The playbook `spec-lifecycle-automation.md`? It only checks help; not stale per se but doesn't cover phase 008; probably no change needed (it's a lifecycle helper help check). Hmm.\n\nI should verify the track-root-children-lists feature catalog for subtrack archive behavior (phase 003) — likely up to date. Let me read it quickly. Also the feature-catalog root to ensure entries."}
