{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-8626dfcaf9e4772f","status":"completed","result":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/track-root-children-lists.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Track-root children lists\"\n3: description: \"Keeps each track root's `children_ids` equal to the packets the track holds, and blocks a push whose list disagrees.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"track root children_ids\"\n6:   - \"refresh-track-roots\"\n7:   - \"sweep-track-roots\"\n8:   - \"track-root pre-push gate\"\n9: version: 2.0.9.0\n10: ---\n11: \n12: # Track-root children lists\n13: \n14: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n15: \n16: A track root is a folder directly under `specs/`, such as `specs/sk-doc/`, that\n17: holds numbered packets and no spec docs of its own. Its `graph-metadata.json`\n18: lists those packets in `children_ids`.\n19: \n20: No packet rule reaches a track root, because validation exempts tracks, and\n21: the graph backfill refuses one as \"not a spec folder\". So nothing kept the list\n22: current. When the feature landed, 15 of 18 track roots listed packets that\n23: disagreed with the folders on disk.\n24: \n25: The feature keeps the list equal to the packets and stops a push that would\n26: publish a list that disagrees.\n27: \n28: ---\n29: \n30: ## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n31: \n32: `refresh-track-roots.mjs` sets a track's `children_ids` to its numbered packet\n33: folders, sorted, and changes no other field. It is dry by default and writes\n34: with `--apply`, and `--track <name>` limits it to one track. A file named like a\n35: packet, a numbered folder without a `spec.md`, an archive folder and an entry\n36: under an earlier identity are not packets. A declared sub-track with missing `graph-metadata.json` is reported as\n37: a pending creation in a dry run; `--apply` seeds its track-root record before\n38: updating `children_ids`. The writer refuses a `graph-metadata.json` symlink and\n39: leaves it unchanged. Empty or unreadable metadata is also left alone and exits\n40: with status 2.\n41: \n42: The writer also seeds a declared sub-track's archive. Git does not track an\n43: empty folder, so when a sub-track has no `z_archive/` at all, a dry run prints\n44: `create z_archive/.gitkeep` as pending and `--apply` creates the folder with an\n45: empty `.gitkeep`. A `z_archive/` that already exists is left as it is, a\n46: `z_archive/` that is a symlink is refused and not written, and a flat track's\n47: archive is never seeded.\n48: \n49: `sweep-track-roots.mjs` reports. It compares the list with the packets as sets,\n50: because a packet renamed on disk leaves both counts equal. With `--rev <commit>`\n51: it reads that commit instead of the working tree, and leaves out a symlinked\n52: track, whose files live in another repository. A packet named more than once is\n53: drift even though the set is unchanged: the sweep names it and the writer\n54: removes the repeat.\n55: \n56: A track that holds numbered packets beside declared sub-tracks is mixed. The\n57: sweep names the flat packets and exits 1, even when the children list is\n58: correct. The writer cannot clear it: each flat packet moves into a sub-track.\n59: In the working tree, a numbered folder without `spec.md` beside sub-tracks is\n60: not a packet. It is usually ignored files a moved packet left behind, so the\n61: sweep prints it as a diagnostic and does not fail.\n62: \n63: A declared sub-track is a container one level below a track: its\n64: `\"level\": \"sub-track\"` description makes it a track root in miniature, with the\n65: identity `<track>/<sub>`. The reader returns it after its track, the writer\n66: refreshes its `children_ids` and the track's in one pass, and the sweep reports\n67: its packets at the same depth as a flat track's. A non-numbered folder without\n68: the declaration is reported once and never promoted, and a symlinked sub-track\n69: is skipped with a diagnostic in both views. In the working tree the sweep also\n70: prints one line for each declared sub-track that has no `z_archive/` folder,\n71: naming `refresh-track-roots.mjs --apply` as the way to seed it. A `--rev` sweep\n72: does not make this check. These diagnostics are advisory to\n73: the sweep and do not change its exit code. `create.sh` uses the same diagnostic\n74: to explain a refusal, then exits with status 1.\n75: \n76: `create.sh --track` scaffolds under a track or one declared sub-track, then\n77: refreshes that root and, for a sub-track, its parent. A declared sub-track with\n78: missing metadata is seeded by the refresh. A flat track without\n79: `graph-metadata.json` remains unrefreshed. If the parent track has no graph metadata,\n80: creation proceeds without refreshing. It exits with status 1 for absolute paths,\n\n(Showing lines 1-80 of 122. Use offset=81 to continue.)\n</content>"}
