t invite a destructive retry.\n68: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n69: - Do NOT retry: **An `--apply` rollback claim**: `relocate.mjs:34` says status 0 after apply means every step landed; status 3 is explicitly a landed move, so the code does not invite a destructive retry.\n70: \n71: ### **P0 classification for the stale exit status**: no data loss or security breach follows; the cost is a misdiagnosed exit, so P1 is the supported ceiling. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n72: - What was tried: **P0 classification for the stale exit status**: no data loss or security breach follows; the cost is a misdiagnosed exit, so P1 is the supported ceiling.\n73: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n74: - Do NOT retry: **P0 classification for the stale exit status**: no data loss or security breach follows; the cost is a misdiagnosed exit, so P1 is the supported ceiling.\n75: \n76: <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n77: ## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n78: - Completed pivots: 0\n79: - Failed pivots: 0\n80: - Audited overrides: 0\n81: - Swept: none yet\n82: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n83: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n84: \n85: ## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n86: [Review angles that were investigated and definitively eliminated]\n87: \n88: ---\n89: \n90: <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n91: ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n92: - Dimension: security. - Focus area: archive search path handling and restore/refusal documentation; does any manifest doc understate a path-safety or refusal boundary introduced in phases 006-010? - Reason: correctness pass found three observable doc/code contradictions; security is the next uncovered dimension and follows the risk order. - Rotation status: D1 correctness covered; D2 security, D3 traceability, D4 maintainability remain. - Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive direct-read pairing of code behaviour to doc lines; carry the same method into the