{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-8f864493ef0da7da","status":"completed","result":".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/README.md:7:  - \"validate spec folder\"\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/README.md:17:`runtime/cli/spec/` owns shell entrypoints for spec folder lifecycle work. It creates packet folders, upgrades documentation levels, validates structure, checks completion state and archives finished or stale folders.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/README.md:23:- Scripts accept explicit spec folder paths and are intended to run from the repository root.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/README.md:35:│ Operator     │ ───▶ │ create.sh      │ ───▶ │ Spec folder    │\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/README.md:59:+-- create.sh                    # Scaffold spec folders from templates\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/README.md:65:+-- scaffold-debug-delegation.sh # Generate debug-delegation handoff scaffolds\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/README.md:68:+-- archive.sh                   # Move completed or stale spec folders\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/README.md:93:- Lifecycle scripts may read templates and write only the selected spec folder. There are two exceptions. `create.sh --track` also lists the new packet in that track root's `children_ids`, and `upgrade-legacy.mjs` writes across every failing packet in the specs roots it is given.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/README.md:107:| `create.sh` | Creates new Level 1 or phase folders from templates. It seeds the trigger phrases of the 15 template document kinds with the packet slug. After the documents are written, it replaces the planned `graph-metadata.json` stub with metadata derived from them through `backfill-graph-metadata.ts`, and a failed derivation warns and leaves the stub in place. With `--track`, it then runs `refresh-track-roots.mjs` for that track, so the new packet is listed in the track root's `children_ids` from the start. |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/README.md:109:| `validate.sh` | Runs the modular validation gate used before completion claims. `resolve_orchestrator()` checks the compiled runtime dist freshness (via `../lib/dist-freshness.cjs`) before trusting it and fails closed with exit `3` when stale: no silent auto-rebuild. A linked `upgrade-baseline.json` is not applied: the validator warns `UPGRADE_BASELINE_LINK` and the findings it would have downgraded stay errors. `--quiet` prints only the result line. `--include-archive` needs `--recursive`, and exits `2` without it. It also validates the packets in the `z_archive/` of the folder given and, for a track root, of each declared sub-track. On a `--strict` run, a Draft packet whose only errors are derived-metadata rules gets one `repair-derived.cjs --apply` and one revalidation, so the run can write files. `SPECKIT_DRAFT_AUTO_REPAIR=0` (or a set `CI`, or a `SPECKIT_RULES` subset) turns that off. |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/README.md:111:| `scaffold-debug-delegation.sh` | Generates `debug-delegation.md` handoff scaffolds from failure-trail input. |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/README.md:114:| `archive.sh` | Moves completed or stale spec folders into the `z_archive/` beside them: `specs/z_archive/` for a packet at the specs root, `specs/<track>/z_archive/` for a packet in a track, the sub-track's own `z_archive/` for a packet in a sub-track and the parent's own `z_archive/` for a phase. `--restore` returns a folder to the place its archive belongs to. When a live packet with another name already holds its number, the restore lands on the next free number above every live and archived packet there, through `relocate.mjs --from <archived> --to <next> --apply`. `--list` shows every archive's entries by the path that restores them. Archives are found beside the specs root, each track, each declared sub-track and the numbered folders beneath them, without following links, so a copy of a specs tree kept in a packet's research is left out. After every move it runs `repair-derived.cjs` over the moved folder, so the packet and each packet inside it record their new path, and in a track it runs `refresh-track-roots.mjs` for that track, so the track root's `children_ids` follows the packet. After an archive or a plain restore it also asks `ensureDescriptionCache` to rebuild the description cache `specs/descriptions.json` when that file exists, so the cache drops the row for the folder that is gone. A failed rebuild warns and leaves the move in place. A phase parent's `graph-metadata.json` is left as it is, because its writer drops a child only through a reviewed prune. A `z_archive/` that is a symlink is refused on archive and on restore, and `--list` leaves a linked archive out without naming it. An archive or restore path with a `.` or `..` segment is refused before anything resolves it. |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/README.md:115:| `is-phase-parent.ts` | Detects whether a folder is a phase parent and reports child-count manifest health. |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/README.md:117:| `sweep-track-roots.mjs` | Sweeps every track root (spec-less directory under `specs/` carrying a `graph-metadata.json`) and compares its declared `children_ids` with the numbered child directories that hold a `spec.md`, one line per track; exits 1 when any track differs or holds numbered packets beside declared sub-tracks. A track matches only when the two sets are equal and no packet is declared more than once: equal counts are not enough, since a renamed packet leaves both counts where they were, and a repeated entry leaves the sets equal. A repeat prints `declared more than once: <names>`. In the working tree, a numbered folder without `spec.md` beside sub-tracks prints `numbered folder without spec.md beside sub-tracks` as an advisory diagnostic. Also in the working tree only, a declared sub-track without a `z_archive/` prints `sub-track has no z_archive/; seed it with refresh-track-roots.mjs --apply`, an advisory diagnostic that never changes the exit code. `--rev <commit>` reads that commit instead of the working tree and leaves out symlinked tracks; the pre-push track-root gate runs it that way. Per-packet validation never reaches a track root, because the orchestrator exempts track directories from packet rules. Read-only. |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/README.md:119:| `repair-derived.cjs` | Repairs derivable packet facts (folder name, packet pointer, level, metadata fingerprint) and refuses authored ones; see `README-repair-derived.md`. A linked rewrite target (`description.json`, `graph-metadata.json` or one of the packet documents) is refused: the run prints `left unchanged <file>: symbolic link, not followed` and writes through no link. A linked `graph-metadata.json` is also never re-derived, so the dry run and `--apply` report the same work. Every `UNREADABLE` line names its reason. |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/README.md:120:| `relocate.mjs` | Moves, renumbers or re-parents spec packets from `--map <file.json>`, `--from` with `--to`, or `--renumber <folder>`, and leaves every store that records a packet path agreeing with the new place. Preflight refuses a destination collision, a taken number (archived siblings count), a track left mixed, a destination deeper than one sub-track, a name that is not `NNN-slug`, a path outside `specs/` or through a link, and uncommitted changes on a path the run would move or rewrite, all before the first write. It then moves each folder (`git mv` when tracked), drops and adds phase-parent `children_ids` for the ids the map names, rewrites every whole old id under `specs/` and recomputes relative markdown links, and drives `migrate-generated-json --only`, `repair-derived.cjs`, `refresh-track-roots.mjs`, `cite-drift-scan.mjs --rebuild-redirects` and `generate-trigger-index.mjs`. Each applied move is appended to `sk-doc/shared/scripts/relocation-ledger.json`, and the run closes with `sweep-track-roots.mjs` and `validate.sh --strict` on each moved packet. A moved path na","truncated":true}
