And line 67 exit codes. One finding with primary line 67.\n\n- F008 (P2): `SKILL.md:317` script list omits relocate.mjs/suggest-subtracks.mjs/archive.sh; the Quick Reference table has no relocation/archive rows. This is the \"SKILL.md never updated\" gap beyond F001. P2 discoverability. But is SKILL.md supposed to list every script? It lists four scripts as examples. The manifest's phase 002 scope said SKILL.md should be modified for subtrack docs; line 287 does mention suggest-subtracks. So SKILL.md got a minimal update. The tool list omission is a gap but maybe not a defect. I'll rate P2 and note that the skill's \"Scripts:\" line is a representative list, not exhaustive. Hmm, if it's not exhaustive, omitting relocate may be acceptable. But the operator focus says SKILL.md never updated for 006-010. The strongest SKILL.md finding is F001 (next-number) and the quick reference omission. I'll include F008 as P2 with a downgrade trigger. Or combine with F001? F001 is the next-number command; F008 is the missing tool rows. Separate.\n\n- F009 (P2): `SKILL.md:295` is already F001. Don't duplicate.\n- F010 (P2): `references/retrieval/retrieval-conventions.md:84` says \"the JSON rows of the structured and count recipes carry archived: true|false\" and doesn't mention the path recipe's `archivedPaths`. Also `.skilled/commands/speckit/search.md:116`, `.skilled/commands/speckit/assets/search-presentation.txt:120`, `.skilled/commands/speckit/README.txt:105`. This is the archivedPaths docs cluster. Primary: retrieval-conventions.md:84 (the retrieval contract). P1 or P2? The phase 009 goal's completion criterion is \"the --json path record marks the same paths\". The docs that describe the JSON record claim only structured/count rows. A consumer of the path recipe's JSON has no documented field. This is a current-state contract gap in the retrieval reference. I'd rate P1 (spec mismatch), but I already have F002/F003/F001 as P1. Is it materially different? Yes, it's the path JSO