rge may expect a terminal synthesis record with that reason when the cap is hit (per the persona's note: \"Under stop_policy=max-iterations, the terminal synthesis record must carry stopReason: maxIterationsReached\"). Our stopPolicy is convergence, but we hit the cap. I'll use maxIterationsReached.\n\n- Resource map: step_emit_resource_map skip_when config.fanout is present. My config has no fanout, so I can run reducer with --emit-resource-map. It will write `resource-map.md` in the lineage. Is that required for the lineage? The fanout runner expects review-report.md. The resource map is optional. The SKILL says review-report has a conditional Resource Map Coverage Gate only if resource_map_present; ours is false. The `resource-map.md` output from converged deltas might be nice but not required. The workflow step_emit_resource_map would run; I'll run it for fidelity. It may produce a resource map based on filesReviewed. Fine, inside lineage.\n- Compile review-report.md with 9 core sections + Planning Packet. I must write it myself (the workflow step is a template instruction). It should include:\n  1 Executive Summary (verdict CONDITIONAL, counts, scope, operator focus verbatim).\n  2 Planning Trigger + fenced json Planning Packet with triggered, verdict, hasAdvisories, activeFindings, remediationWorkstreams, specSeed, planSeed, findingClasses, affectedSurfacesSeed, fixCompletenessRequired.\n  3 Active Finding Registry (all 15, with ID, severity, title, dimension, file:line, evidence, impact, fix recommendation, disposition, findingClass, scopeProof, affectedSurfaceHints).\n  4 Remediation Workstreams (P1 first, then P2).\n  5 Spec Seed.\n  6 Plan Seed.\n  7 Traceability Status (core/overlay; AC_COVERAGE exempt/disabled — the target is Level 2 phase parent; does acceptance-criteria.md exist at parent? The parent has no acceptance-criteria.md (ls showed none). The child 005 has acceptance-criteria? The target is the parent spec folder; AC_COVERAGE signal for parent: if level 2+ and acceptance-criteria.md exists and implementation-summary in progress. The parent has no acceptance-criteria.md, so exempt. I'll state \"exempt (no parent acceptance-criteria.md; phase children carry their own)\".)\n  8 Deferred Items (P2 advisories).\n  9 Search Ledger (no v2 search-depth state captured; legacy v1 record).\n  10 Audit Appendix.\n  - Optional Resource Map Coverage Gate: resource_map_present false, so skip/note.\n  - Dimension Expansion Map after Deferred Items and before Search Ledger (workflow says insert it). I'll include.\n- Convergence report via synthesis-closeout.cjs: It stages events, then I must run the gateway for each event. It uses artifact dir, state log, registry, output, dashboard, stop reason, counts, dimension coverage, verdict, release readiness. It reads the registry and state logs, writes? Let me inspect what it does with output/dashboard: it may validate the report and dashboard exist, then stage convergence events. It doesn't write the report. It may write to `artifactDir`? Let me check the rest of the script. It likely stages `convergence_report` events. It may update the dashboard. Let me read the relevant portion 320-420."}
