gnment, WS4 catalog/playbook refresh)\n5 Spec Seed\n6 Plan Seed\n7 Traceability Status (+ AC_COVERAGE exempt)\n8 Deferred Items (P2s)\nDimension Expansion Map\n9 Search Ledger (legacy v1)\n10 Audit Appendix\nMaybe Resource Map Coverage Gate section? resource_map_present false → omit, per contract. But the SKILL says report has 9 core sections plus conditional; I'll include a note in Traceability or Audit that resource map was absent. The section should not be present if false. Fine.\n\nPlanning Packet:\n```json\n{\n  \"triggered\": true,\n  \"verdict\": \"CONDITIONAL\",\n  \"hasAdvisories\": false,\n  \"activeFindings\": [\n    {\"id\":\"F001\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"title\":\"...\",\"file\":\"...\",\"findingClass\":\"cross-consumer\"},\n    ...\n  ],\n  \"remediationWorkstreams\": [\n    {\"id\":\"WS1\",\"priority\":\"P1\",\"findingIds\":[\"F001\"],\"goal\":\"...\"},\n    ...\n  ],\n  \"specSeed\": [\"...\"],\n  \"planSeed\": [\"...\"],\n  \"findingClasses\": [\"cross-consumer\",\"instance-only\"],\n  \"affectedSurfacesSeed\": [\"SKILL.md\",\"feature catalog\",\"references\",\"changelog\",\"playbooks\",\"CLI README\"],\n  \"fixCompletenessRequired\": true\n}\n```\n`activeFindings` must be from reducer-owned state plus iteration findingDetails; all 15. Good.\n\nVerdict CONDITIONAL; hasAdvisories false (only true when PASS + P2). The workflow's `step_derive_verdict` says has_advisories = (verdict == PASS and p2_count > 0). Since CONDITIONAL, false. Good.\n\nResource map: run `reduce-state.cjs --emit-resource-map` before writing the report? The resource map output may include a file list; the report doesn't need it because resource_map_present false. But the workflow step emits it. I'll run it after the report maybe. It will write `resource-map.md` in lineage. Fine.\n\nConvergence report: run synthesis-closeout with:\n- --mode review\n- --event-dir <lineage>/.synthesis-events (inside lineage)\n- --artifact-dir <lineage>\n- --state-log <lineage>/deep-review-state.jsonl\n- --registry <lineage>/deep-review-findings-registry.json\n- --output <lineage>/review-report.md\n- --dashboard <lineage>/deep-review-dashboard.md\n- --stop-reason maxIterationsReached\n- --active-p0 0 --active-p1 4 --active-p2 11\n- --dimension-coverage 1\n- --verdict CONDITIONAL\n- --release-readiness-state in-progress\nThen send each event file to gateway.\n\nThen update config status complete (terminal flip) and rerun reducer to refresh dashboard. But careful: the reducer after the terminal synthesis might change strategy/dashboard only; no new ledger records. Fine.\n\nAlso the fanout runner expects `review-report.md` and `deep-review-state.jsonl` with gateway frames. We'll have those.\n\nLet me write the report. I'll include all 15 findings with evidence and fixes, but keep it readable.\n\nRemediation Workstreams:\n- WS1 (P1): Exit and restore contracts — F001, F002, F003. Update SKILL.md next-number, relocation catalog status 3, lifecycle catalog restore verdict/mixed track.\n- WS2 (P1): Archive JSON contract — F005. Document `archivedPaths` in retrieval-conventions, search.md, search-presentation, README.txt; propagate to feature catalog (F011) and playbooks (F014).\n- WS3 (P2): Reference alignment — F004, F006, F007, F008, F009, F010, F015.\n- WS4 (P2): Catalog/playbook refresh — F011-F015 (some overlap) — maybe WS3/WS4 split by doc family:\n  - WS3: Reference and SKILL.md alignment (F004, F006, F007, F008, F015).\n  - WS4: Changelog and catalog current-state refresh (F009, F010, F011).\n  - WS5: Playbook scenario coverage (F012, F013, F014).\n- The P1 set is WS1+WS2.\n\nSpec seed: bullets for spec.md scope/files to change (docs now part of packet); note parent spec \"Files to Change\" needs rows for docs; and decision-record amendment? The completion criterion's docs are part of the skill, not spec. The spec seed should say \"add doc-update rows to parent spec.md for phase 011 or a follow-up\" etc.\n\nPlan seed: tasks to fix docs.\n\nTraceability status:\n- spec_code core partial (4 P1s)\n- checklist_evidence core pass\n- skill_agent overlay notApplicable (no agent definition in manifest)\n- agent_cross_runtime notApplicable\n- feature_catalog_code partial\n- playbook_capability partial\n- AC_COVERAGE exempt (no parent acceptance-criteria.md; phase children carry their own).\n\nAudit appendix: 5 iterations, ratios 1.0, 0.0625, 0.36, 0.1667, 0.0323; stop reason maxIterationsReached; dimensions covered 4/4; files reviewed 74? Actually we didn't read all 74 files. We reviewed the major docs and code; but the scope is all 74. Did we ignore many? We read key docs and code; not all 74. The report should be honest: the review covered the behavioural surfaces and sampled/read the manifest docs; not every one of the 74 paths was opened. Hmm. The scope discovery sets scope = all 74 manifest paths; the review should cover them. We did not read all 74 (e.g., .env.example, agents-md-manifest.json, some presentations, tests). The operator focus was docs alignment, and we covered the docs. For the coverage claim, I should say \"scope 74; read/spot-checked the behavioural surfaces and the full documentation set; 15 doc findings; test/config files outside the documentation focus were not exhaustively read.\" That's honest but may weaken \"dimensions covered\". The iteration records list filesReviewed; the union is ~40. The audit appendix can report the exact count of files/line ranges read. I'll count roughly and say \"the review read the code producers and every manifest documentation page that states the phase 006-010 behaviour; the remaining manifest entries are tests, presentations and config files checked only as supporting anchors.\" That's a declared limit, not a silent pass. The completion criteria for the review lineage are about artifacts, not coverage. Fine.\n\nLet me write the report now. It's long; I'll produce it with the write tool.\n\nOne more thing: the final verdict in the report must be consistent: CONDITIONAL. The